window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/a492-589595d39f0c47ca.json"]={sha256:"589595d39f0c47ca1a91895f4fbb746440dd63346aadc446f014e188e2b6cd85",value:{"id":"a492","title":"ESO 甚大望遠鏡 VLT","titleEn":"ESO Very Large Telescope","category":"instruments","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"以 Paranal 山頂四座 8.2 m 單元望遠鏡為對象，從視寧度與繞射的差距出發，拆解 Ritchey–Chrétien 光路與多焦點、177 mm 薄 Zerodur 主鏡製作、1170 致動器可變形副鏡、四雷射導引星、VLTI 延遲線與 ESPRESSO 的 10 cm/s 量測，最後整合成多望遠鏡的營運交接。","summaryEn":"Taking the four 8.2 m Unit Telescopes on Cerro Paranal, start from the gap between seeing and diffraction and work through the Ritchey–Chrétien train and its foci, the 177 mm thin Zerodur primary, the 1170-actuator deformable secondary, four laser guide stars, VLTI delay lines and ESPRESSO's 10 cm/s measurement, ending in a multi-telescope operational handoff.","scope":"依公開物理原理與官方資料編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是原廠配方、施工圖、設備操作許可或安全程序。數值均為教學假設，需依實際規格重算。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public physics and official sources. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not vendor recipes, construction drawings, operating authorisation or safety procedures. Numbers are teaching assumptions and must be recalculated for real specifications.","subcategory":"optics-facilities-observatories","subcategoryTitle":"大型望遠鏡與重力波觀測站","subcategoryTitleEn":"Large telescopes and gravitational-wave observatories","learningTrack":"optics","learningSubdiscipline":"optics-facilities-observatories","learningTags":["optics","optics-facilities-observatories","telescope"],"architectureFamily":"telescope","architectureNodes":[["8.2 m 薄主鏡與主動支撐","8.2 m thin primary and active support"],["可變形副鏡","Deformable secondary mirror"],["四雷射導引星","Four laser guide stars"],["Nasmyth 與 Cassegrain 儀器","Nasmyth and Cassegrain instruments"],["VLTI 延遲線與合光器","VLTI delay lines and combiners"],["合併 coudé 與 ESPRESSO","Combined coudé and ESPRESSO"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[2,1],[1,3],[1,4],[1,5]],"diagram":{"type":"telescope","labels":["8.2 m 薄主鏡與主動支撐","可變形副鏡","四雷射導引星","Nasmyth 與 Cassegrain 儀器","VLTI 延遲線與合光器"],"labelsEn":["8.2 m thin primary and active support","Deformable secondary mirror","Four laser guide stars","Nasmyth and Cassegrain instruments","VLTI delay lines and combiners"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"UT4 自適應光學 K 波段練習：假設 500 nm 的 r₀ = 0.15 m，換算到 2.2 µm 為 r₀ = 0.15 × (2.2/0.5)^1.2 ≈ 0.89 m。擬合誤差以投影間距 0.205 m 計 σ_fit² ≈ 0.28 × (0.205/0.89)^5/3 ≈ 0.024 rad²；風速 15 m/s 時 Greenwood 頻率 f_G = 0.427v/r₀ ≈ 7.2 Hz，假設修正頻寬 60 Hz，時間誤差 σ_t² = (7.2/60)^5/3 ≈ 0.029 rad²；另給雜訊與混疊 0.03 rad²。總和 0.084 rad²，Strehl ≈ exp(−0.084) ≈ 0.92。修正後影像寬約 λ/D ≈ 55 mas，而 K 波段未修正視寧度約 0.50″，相差約 9 倍。數值為教學假設，不代表 VLT 的實際規格。","textEn":"UT4 adaptive-optics exercise in K band: assume r₀ = 0.15 m at 500 nm, which scales to r₀ = 0.15 × (2.2/0.5)^1.2 ≈ 0.89 m at 2.2 µm. With a projected pitch of 0.205 m the fitting error is σ_fit² ≈ 0.28 × (0.205/0.89)^5/3 ≈ 0.024 rad²; for a 15 m/s wind the Greenwood frequency is f_G = 0.427v/r₀ ≈ 7.2 Hz, and with an assumed 60 Hz correction bandwidth the temporal error is σ_t² = (7.2/60)^5/3 ≈ 0.029 rad²; allow 0.03 rad² for noise and aliasing. The total is 0.084 rad² and Strehl ≈ exp(−0.084) ≈ 0.92. The corrected image is about λ/D ≈ 55 mas wide, against about 0.50″ of uncorrected K-band seeing, a factor of about 9. Values are teaching assumptions, not VLT specifications.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表實機量測、產品額定或操作參數；改變系統邊界後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not measured hardware, product ratings or operating parameters; recalculate after changing the system boundary.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與設施背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and facility context, not these numbers."},"depth":4,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":12,"enrichmentVersion":12,"stages":[{"id":"a492-v12-s1","title":"系統邊界與物理原理","titleEn":"System boundaries and physical principles","description":"本階段聚焦「集光、視寧度與繞射的系統邊界」與「RC 光學、副鏡五軸與多焦點配置」：先建立機制與定量模型，再設計驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Light grasp, seeing and diffraction as the system boundary\" and \"RC optics, the five-axis secondary and multiple foci\": build the mechanism and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"a492-v12-01","title":"集光、視寧度與繞射的系統邊界：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Light grasp, seeing and diffraction as the system boundary: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「四座 8.2 m 單元望遠鏡」如何決定ESO 甚大望遠鏡 VLT的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Four 8.2 m Unit Telescopes” determines the key performance of “ESO Very Large Telescope”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"VLT 由四座 8.2 m 單元望遠鏡、四座可移動的 1.8 m 輔助望遠鏡與地下干涉實驗室組成，涵蓋近紫外到 25 µm。口徑帶來兩種好處：集光面積讓暗弱天體在有限時間內達到訊雜比，角解析度則理論上隨 λ/D 變好；但大氣湍流把波前切成尺寸約 Fried 參數 r₀ 的同調區塊，未修正時影像寬度由 λ/r₀ 決定，與口徑無關。因此 VLT 的工程設計一直沿著兩條線前進：把四座望遠鏡的光合在一起增加集光或基線，以及以主動與自適應光學把影像拉回繞射極限。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「四座 8.2 m 單元望遠鏡」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The VLT comprises four 8.2 m Unit Telescopes, four relocatable 1.8 m Auxiliary Telescopes and an underground interferometric laboratory, covering the near ultraviolet to 25 µm. Aperture brings two benefits: collecting area lets faint targets reach a useful signal-to-noise ratio in finite time, and angular resolution in principle improves as λ/D. Atmospheric turbulence, however, breaks the wavefront into coherent patches of about the Fried parameter r₀, so the uncorrected image width is set by λ/r₀ regardless of aperture. VLT engineering has therefore advanced along two lines: combining the four telescopes for more collecting area or longer baselines, and using active and adaptive optics to pull images back toward the diffraction limit. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Four 8.2 m Unit Telescopes”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：取 r₀ = 0.15 m（500 nm，假設），視寧度 FWHM ≈ 0.98λ/r₀ ≈ 0.67″，而 8.2 m 的繞射極限 1.22λ/D ≈ 15 mas，差 40 倍以上；D/r₀ ≈ 55，瞳面約含 (D/r₀)² ≈ 3000 個同調區塊。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Take r₀ = 0.15 m at 500 nm (assumption): seeing FWHM ≈ 0.98λ/r₀ ≈ 0.67″, while the 8.2 m diffraction limit 1.22λ/D ≈ 15 mas is more than 40 times smaller; D/r₀ ≈ 55, so the pupil holds about (D/r₀)² ≈ 3000 coherent patches.","failure":"常見誤解：「望遠鏡口徑加倍，地面影像的解析度就一定加倍。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Doubling the aperture always doubles the resolution of ground-based images.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「四座 8.2 m 單元望遠鏡」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Four 8.2 m Unit Telescopes”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a492-v12-01-k1","title":"集光、視寧度與繞射的系統邊界","titleEn":"Light grasp, seeing and diffraction as the system boundary","text":"VLT 由四座 8.2 m 單元望遠鏡、四座可移動的 1.8 m 輔助望遠鏡與地下干涉實驗室組成，涵蓋近紫外到 25 µm。口徑帶來兩種好處：集光面積讓暗弱天體在有限時間內達到訊雜比，角解析度則理論上隨 λ/D 變好；但大氣湍流把波前切成尺寸約 Fried 參數 r₀ 的同調區塊，未修正時影像寬度由 λ/r₀ 決定，與口徑無關。","textEn":"The VLT comprises four 8.2 m Unit Telescopes, four relocatable 1.8 m Auxiliary Telescopes and an underground interferometric laboratory, covering the near ultraviolet to 25 µm. Aperture brings two benefits: collecting area lets faint targets reach a useful signal-to-noise ratio in finite time, and angular resolution in principle improves as λ/D.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]},{"id":"a492-v12-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：望遠鏡口徑加倍，地面影像的解析度就一定加倍。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Doubling the aperture always doubles the resolution of ground-based images. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「集光、視寧度與繞射的系統邊界」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Light grasp, seeing and diffraction as the system boundary\" is correct?","options":["望遠鏡口徑加倍，地面影像的解析度就一定加倍。","VLT 由四座 8.2 m 單元望遠鏡、四座可移動的 1.8 m 輔助望遠鏡與地下干涉實驗室組成，涵蓋近紫外到 25 µm。","副鏡只是轉折光路的鏡子，位置差幾十微米沒有影響。"],"optionsEn":["Doubling the aperture always doubles the resolution of ground-based images.","The VLT comprises four 8.2 m Unit Telescopes, four relocatable 1.8 m Auxiliary Telescopes and an underground interferometric laboratory, covering the near ultraviolet to 25 µm.","The secondary only folds the beam, so tens of micrometres of position error do not matter."],"answer":1,"explanation":"VLT 由四座 8.2 m 單元望遠鏡、四座可移動的 1.8 m 輔助望遠鏡與地下干涉實驗室組成，涵蓋近紫外到 25 µm。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The VLT comprises four 8.2 m Unit Telescopes, four relocatable 1.8 m Auxiliary Telescopes and an underground interferometric laboratory, covering the near ultraviolet to 25 µm. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"a492-v12-02","title":"集光、視寧度與繞射的系統邊界：定量估算","titleEn":"Light grasp, seeing and diffraction as the system boundary: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"],"prerequisiteIds":["a492-v12-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「四座 8.2 m 單元望遠鏡」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Four 8.2 m Unit Telescopes” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：取 r₀ = 0.15 m（500 nm，假設），視寧度 FWHM ≈ 0.98λ/r₀ ≈ 0.67″，而 8.2 m 的繞射極限 1.22λ/D ≈ 15 mas，差 40 倍以上；D/r₀ ≈ 55，瞳面約含 (D/r₀)² ≈ 3000 個同調區塊。四座 UT 非同調合光的等效口徑為 √4 × 8.2 m = 16.4 m。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Take r₀ = 0.15 m at 500 nm (assumption): seeing FWHM ≈ 0.98λ/r₀ ≈ 0.67″, while the 8.2 m diffraction limit 1.22λ/D ≈ 15 mas is more than 40 times smaller; D/r₀ ≈ 55, so the pupil holds about (D/r₀)² ≈ 3000 coherent patches. Incoherently combining the four UTs gives an equivalent aperture of √4 × 8.2 m = 16.4 m. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：以差分影像運動監測器（DIMM）量 r₀ 與視寧度，並同時記錄望遠鏡導星相機的影像 FWHM；把兩者換算到相同波長與天頂角（FWHM ∝ λ^−1/5、∝ sec z^3/5）比較，差額即為望遠鏡本身與圓頂的貢獻，再與影像品質預算比對。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure r₀ and seeing with a differential image-motion monitor (DIMM) while logging image FWHM from the telescope guide camera; convert both to the same wavelength and zenith angle (FWHM ∝ λ^−1/5 and ∝ sec z^3/5) and compare, treating the difference as the telescope and enclosure contribution to be checked against the image-quality budget.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a492-v12-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"取 r₀ = 0.15 m（500 nm，假設），視寧度 FWHM ≈ 0.98λ/r₀ ≈ 0.67″，而 8.2 m 的繞射極限 1.22λ/D ≈ 15 mas，差 40 倍以上；D/r₀ ≈ 55，瞳面約含 (D/r₀)² ≈ 3000 個同調區塊。四座 UT 非同調合光的等效口徑為 √4 × 8.2 m = 16.4 m。","textEn":"Take r₀ = 0.15 m at 500 nm (assumption): seeing FWHM ≈ 0.98λ/r₀ ≈ 0.67″, while the 8.2 m diffraction limit 1.22λ/D ≈ 15 mas is more than 40 times smaller; D/r₀ ≈ 55, so the pupil holds about (D/r₀)² ≈ 3000 coherent patches. Incoherently combining the four UTs gives an equivalent aperture of √4 × 8.2 m = 16.4 m.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]},{"id":"a492-v12-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「集光、視寧度與繞射的系統邊界」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Light grasp, seeing and diffraction as the system boundary\", which statement holds?","options":["致動器越多越好，與觀測波長無關。","只要基線夠長，干涉儀的角解析度就自動實現，與光程穩定度無關。","取 r₀ = 0.15 m（500 nm，假設），視寧度 FWHM ≈ 0.98λ/r₀ ≈ 0.67″，而 8.2 m 的繞射極限 1.22λ/D ≈ 15 mas，差 40 倍以上。"],"optionsEn":["More actuators are always better, regardless of the observing wavelength.","With a long enough baseline the interferometer's resolution is achieved automatically, regardless of path stability.","Take r₀ = 0.15 m at 500 nm (assumption): seeing FWHM ≈ 0.98λ/r₀ ≈ 0.67″, while the 8.2 m diffraction limit 1.22λ/D ≈ 15 mas is more than 40 times smaller."],"answer":2,"explanation":"取 r₀ = 0.15 m（500 nm，假設），視寧度 FWHM ≈ 0.98λ/r₀ ≈ 0.67″，而 8.2 m 的繞射極限 1.22λ/D ≈ 15 mas，差 40 倍以上；D/r₀ ≈ 55，瞳面約含 (D/r₀)² ≈ 3000 個同調區塊。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Take r₀ = 0.15 m at 500 nm (assumption): seeing FWHM ≈ 0.98λ/r₀ ≈ 0.67″, while the 8.2 m diffraction limit 1.22λ/D ≈ 15 mas is more than 40 times smaller; D/r₀ ≈ 55, so the pupil holds about (D/r₀)² ≈ 3000 coherent patches. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"a492-v12-03","title":"集光、視寧度與繞射的系統邊界：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Light grasp, seeing and diffraction as the system boundary: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"],"prerequisiteIds":["a492-v12-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「四座 8.2 m 單元望遠鏡」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Four 8.2 m Unit Telescopes” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"以差分影像運動監測器（DIMM）量 r₀ 與視寧度，並同時記錄望遠鏡導星相機的影像 FWHM；把兩者換算到相同波長與天頂角（FWHM ∝ λ^−1/5、∝ sec z^3/5）比較，差額即為望遠鏡本身與圓頂的貢獻，再與影像品質預算比對。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure r₀ and seeing with a differential image-motion monitor (DIMM) while logging image FWHM from the telescope guide camera; convert both to the same wavelength and zenith angle (FWHM ∝ λ^−1/5 and ∝ sec z^3/5) and compare, treating the difference as the telescope and enclosure contribution to be checked against the image-quality budget. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：若只看口徑而忽略站址與局部湍流，8 m 級望遠鏡的影像會和 1 m 級望遠鏡一樣寬，只多了集光；更常見的是把圓頂內熱湍流誤當成大氣視寧度，導致錯誤地升級光學而非改善熱控。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: Judging a telescope by aperture alone, without site and local turbulence, leaves an 8 m class telescope with images as wide as a 1 m telescope and only more light; more commonly, dome thermal turbulence is mistaken for atmospheric seeing and the optics are upgraded instead of the thermal control.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a492-v12-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以差分影像運動監測器（DIMM）量 r₀ 與視寧度，並同時記錄望遠鏡導星相機的影像 FWHM；把兩者換算到相同波長與天頂角（FWHM ∝ λ^−1/5、∝ sec z^3/5）比較，差額即為望遠鏡本身與圓頂的貢獻，再與影像品質預算比對。","textEn":"Measure r₀ and seeing with a differential image-motion monitor (DIMM) while logging image FWHM from the telescope guide camera; convert both to the same wavelength and zenith angle (FWHM ∝ λ^−1/5 and ∝ sec z^3/5) and compare, treating the difference as the telescope and enclosure contribution to be checked against the image-quality budget.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]},{"id":"a492-v12-03-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「集光、視寧度與繞射的系統邊界」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Light grasp, seeing and diffraction as the system boundary\"?","options":["以差分影像運動監測器（DIMM）量 r₀ 與視寧度，並同時記錄望遠鏡導星相機的影像 FWHM。","量測時不必記錄溫度、振動與時間等條件，因為它們不會影響結果。","只要解析度夠高，徑向速度精度就不受儀器穩定度限制。"],"optionsEn":["Measure r₀ and seeing with a differential image-motion monitor (DIMM) while logging image FWHM from the telescope guide camera.","Temperature, vibration and timing need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","With high enough resolving power, radial-velocity precision is not limited by instrument stability."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以差分影像運動監測器（DIMM）量 r₀ 與視寧度，並同時記錄望遠鏡導星相機的影像 FWHM；把兩者換算到相同波長與天頂角（FWHM ∝ λ^−1/5、∝ sec z^3/5）比較，差額即為望遠鏡本身與圓頂的貢獻，再與影像品質預算比對。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure r₀ and seeing with a differential image-motion monitor (DIMM) while logging image FWHM from the telescope guide camera; convert both to the same wavelength and zenith angle (FWHM ∝ λ^−1/5 and ∝ sec z^3/5) and compare, treating the difference as the telescope and enclosure contribution to be checked against the image-quality budget. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"a492-v12-04","title":"集光、視寧度與繞射的系統邊界：失效診斷","titleEn":"Light grasp, seeing and diffraction as the system boundary: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"],"prerequisiteIds":["a492-v12-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「四座 8.2 m 單元望遠鏡」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Four 8.2 m Unit Telescopes” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"若只看口徑而忽略站址與局部湍流，8 m 級望遠鏡的影像會和 1 m 級望遠鏡一樣寬，只多了集光；更常見的是把圓頂內熱湍流誤當成大氣視寧度，導致錯誤地升級光學而非改善熱控。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"Judging a telescope by aperture alone, without site and local turbulence, leaves an 8 m class telescope with images as wide as a 1 m telescope and only more light; more commonly, dome thermal turbulence is mistaken for atmospheric seeing and the optics are upgraded instead of the thermal control. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：因此 VLT 的工程設計一直沿著兩條線前進：把四座望遠鏡的光合在一起增加集光或基線，以及以主動與自適應光學把影像拉回繞射極限。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: VLT engineering has therefore advanced along two lines: combining the four telescopes for more collecting area or longer baselines, and using active and adaptive optics to pull images back toward the diffraction limit.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「望遠鏡口徑加倍，地面影像的解析度就一定加倍。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Doubling the aperture always doubles the resolution of ground-based images.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a492-v12-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若只看口徑而忽略站址與局部湍流，8 m 級望遠鏡的影像會和 1 m 級望遠鏡一樣寬，只多了集光；更常見的是把圓頂內熱湍流誤當成大氣視寧度，導致錯誤地升級光學而非改善熱控。","textEn":"Judging a telescope by aperture alone, without site and local turbulence, leaves an 8 m class telescope with images as wide as a 1 m telescope and only more light; more commonly, dome thermal turbulence is mistaken for atmospheric seeing and the optics are upgraded instead of the thermal control.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]},{"id":"a492-v12-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「集光、視寧度與繞射的系統邊界」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Light grasp, seeing and diffraction as the system boundary\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自操作人員失誤，系統設計不需要檢討。","若只看口徑而忽略站址與局部湍流，8 m 級望遠鏡的影像會和 1 m 級望遠鏡一樣寬，只多了集光。","副鏡只是轉折光路的鏡子，位置差幾十微米沒有影響。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is operator error, so the system design never needs review.","Judging a telescope by aperture alone, without site and local turbulence, leaves an 8 m class telescope with images as wide as a 1 m telescope and only more light.","The secondary only folds the beam, so tens of micrometres of position error do not matter."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若只看口徑而忽略站址與局部湍流，8 m 級望遠鏡的影像會和 1 m 級望遠鏡一樣寬，只多了集光；更常見的是把圓頂內熱湍流誤當成大氣視寧度，導致錯誤地升級光學而非改善熱控。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Judging a telescope by aperture alone, without site and local turbulence, leaves an 8 m class telescope with images as wide as a 1 m telescope and only more light; more commonly, dome thermal turbulence is mistaken for atmospheric seeing and the optics are upgraded instead of the thermal control. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"a492-v12-05","title":"RC 光學、副鏡五軸與多焦點配置：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"RC optics, the five-axis secondary and multiple foci: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"],"prerequisiteIds":["a492-v12-04"],"objective":"說明「Ritchey–Chrétien 光路與焦點」如何決定ESO 甚大望遠鏡 VLT的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Ritchey–Chrétien train and foci” determines the key performance of “ESO Very Large Telescope”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"每座 UT 為 Ritchey–Chrétien 設計：f/1.8 的薄主鏡與剛性輕量化的凸雙曲面副鏡共同消除球差與彗差，經地平式機架指向全天。光可以送到主鏡下方的 Cassegrain 焦點、兩側的 Nasmyth 焦點，或再經轉折送到地下的 coudé 焦點，讓大型穩定儀器固定不動。副鏡單元以五個自由度定位：一軸對焦、兩軸置中、兩軸指向；因為副鏡把主鏡焦比放大約 8 倍，副鏡的微小軸向位移會在焦面被放大，所以副鏡對焦是主動光學閉環中最頻繁的修正。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「Ritchey–Chrétien 光路與焦點」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Each UT is a Ritchey–Chrétien design: an f/1.8 thin primary and a rigid, lightweight convex hyperboloidal secondary jointly cancel spherical aberration and coma, pointed over the whole sky by an alt-azimuth mount. Light can go to the Cassegrain focus below the primary, to the two Nasmyth foci at the sides, or be relayed to a coudé focus in the basement so that large, stable instruments stay fixed. The secondary unit is positioned in five degrees of freedom: one for focus, two for centring and two for pointing. Because the secondary magnifies the primary focal ratio about eightfold, small axial secondary motions are amplified at the focal plane, which makes secondary focus the most frequent correction in the active-optics loop. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Ritchey–Chrétien train and foci”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：主鏡曲率半徑約 28.8 m，焦距 14.4 m，焦比 14.4/8.2 ≈ f/1.76。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The primary radius of curvature is about 28.8 m, so f = 14.4 m and the focal ratio is 14.4/8.2 ≈ f/1.76.","failure":"常見誤解：「副鏡只是轉折光路的鏡子，位置差幾十微米沒有影響。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The secondary only folds the beam, so tens of micrometres of position error do not matter.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「Ritchey–Chrétien 光路與焦點」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Ritchey–Chrétien train and foci”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a492-v12-05-k1","title":"RC 光學、副鏡五軸與多焦點配置","titleEn":"RC optics, the five-axis secondary and multiple foci","text":"每座 UT 為 Ritchey–Chrétien 設計：f/1.8 的薄主鏡與剛性輕量化的凸雙曲面副鏡共同消除球差與彗差，經地平式機架指向全天。光可以送到主鏡下方的 Cassegrain 焦點、兩側的 Nasmyth 焦點，或再經轉折送到地下的 coudé 焦點，讓大型穩定儀器固定不動。","textEn":"Each UT is a Ritchey–Chrétien design: an f/1.8 thin primary and a rigid, lightweight convex hyperboloidal secondary jointly cancel spherical aberration and coma, pointed over the whole sky by an alt-azimuth mount. Light can go to the Cassegrain focus below the primary, to the two Nasmyth foci at the sides, or be relayed to a coudé focus in the basement so that large, stable instruments stay fixed.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]},{"id":"a492-v12-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：副鏡只是轉折光路的鏡子，位置差幾十微米沒有影響。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The secondary only folds the beam, so tens of micrometres of position error do not matter. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「RC 光學、副鏡五軸與多焦點配置」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"RC optics, the five-axis secondary and multiple foci\" is correct?","options":["副鏡只是轉折光路的鏡子，位置差幾十微米沒有影響。","主鏡越厚越剛，影像品質就一定越好。","每座 UT 為 Ritchey–Chrétien 設計：f/1.8 的薄主鏡與剛性輕量化的凸雙曲面副鏡共同消除球差與彗差，經地平式機架指向全天。"],"optionsEn":["The secondary only folds the beam, so tens of micrometres of position error do not matter.","A thicker, stiffer primary always gives better image quality.","Each UT is a Ritchey–Chrétien design: an f/1.8 thin primary and a rigid, lightweight convex hyperboloidal secondary jointly cancel spherical aberration and coma, pointed over the whole sky by an alt-azimuth mount."],"answer":2,"explanation":"每座 UT 為 Ritchey–Chrétien 設計：f/1.8 的薄主鏡與剛性輕量化的凸雙曲面副鏡共同消除球差與彗差，經地平式機架指向全天。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Each UT is a Ritchey–Chrétien design: an f/1.8 thin primary and a rigid, lightweight convex hyperboloidal secondary jointly cancel spherical aberration and coma, pointed over the whole sky by an alt-azimuth mount. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"a492-v12-06","title":"RC 光學、副鏡五軸與多焦點配置：定量估算","titleEn":"RC optics, the five-axis secondary and multiple foci: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"],"prerequisiteIds":["a492-v12-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「Ritchey–Chrétien 光路與焦點」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Ritchey–Chrétien train and foci” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：主鏡曲率半徑約 28.8 m，焦距 14.4 m，焦比 14.4/8.2 ≈ f/1.76。若 Nasmyth 焦比約 f/15，副鏡放大率 m ≈ 15/1.76 ≈ 8.5，焦面位移 ≈ (m² + 1)·Δz ≈ 74·Δz：副鏡移動 10 µm 使焦點移 0.74 mm，而 500 nm 的焦深 ±2λN² 只有 ±0.23 mm。等效焦距 123 m 對應底片比例尺 ≈ 1.68″/mm。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The primary radius of curvature is about 28.8 m, so f = 14.4 m and the focal ratio is 14.4/8.2 ≈ f/1.76. With a Nasmyth ratio near f/15 the secondary magnification is m ≈ 15/1.76 ≈ 8.5 and the focal shift is ≈ (m² + 1)·Δz ≈ 74·Δz: a 10 µm secondary move shifts focus by 0.74 mm, while the 500 nm depth of focus ±2λN² is only ±0.23 mm. The 123 m effective focal length gives a plate scale ≈ 1.68″/mm. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：在 Nasmyth 焦面以波前感測器做副鏡對焦掃描，量離焦項對副鏡位移的斜率，與 (m² + 1) 的預測比較；再以已知角距的星對量測底片比例尺，並在不同仰角重複，分離重力撓曲造成的置中與彗差。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Run a secondary focus scan with the wavefront sensor at the Nasmyth focus, measure the slope of the defocus term versus secondary displacement and compare it with the (m² + 1) prediction; then measure plate scale on star pairs of known separation and repeat at several elevations to separate gravity-flexure-induced decentre and coma.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a492-v12-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"主鏡曲率半徑約 28.8 m，焦距 14.4 m，焦比 14.4/8.2 ≈ f/1.76。若 Nasmyth 焦比約 f/15，副鏡放大率 m ≈ 15/1.76 ≈ 8.5，焦面位移 ≈ (m² + 1)·Δz ≈ 74·Δz：副鏡移動 10 µm 使焦點移 0.74 mm，而 500 nm 的焦深 ±2λN² 只有 ±0.23 mm。等效焦距 123 m 對應底片比例尺 ≈ 1.68″/mm。","textEn":"The primary radius of curvature is about 28.8 m, so f = 14.4 m and the focal ratio is 14.4/8.2 ≈ f/1.76. With a Nasmyth ratio near f/15 the secondary magnification is m ≈ 15/1.76 ≈ 8.5 and the focal shift is ≈ (m² + 1)·Δz ≈ 74·Δz: a 10 µm secondary move shifts focus by 0.74 mm, while the 500 nm depth of focus ±2λN² is only ±0.23 mm. The 123 m effective focal length gives a plate scale ≈ 1.68″/mm.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]},{"id":"a492-v12-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「RC 光學、副鏡五軸與多焦點配置」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"RC optics, the five-axis secondary and multiple foci\", which statement holds?","options":["主鏡曲率半徑約 28.8 m，焦距 14.4 m，焦比 14.4/8.2 ≈ f/1.76。","有了雷射導引星就完全不需要自然星。","只要解析度夠高，徑向速度精度就不受儀器穩定度限制。"],"optionsEn":["The primary radius of curvature is about 28.8 m, so f = 14.4 m and the focal ratio is 14.4/8.2 ≈ f/1.76.","With laser guide stars no natural star is needed at all.","With high enough resolving power, radial-velocity precision is not limited by instrument stability."],"answer":0,"explanation":"主鏡曲率半徑約 28.8 m，焦距 14.4 m，焦比 14.4/8.2 ≈ f/1.76。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The primary radius of curvature is about 28.8 m, so f = 14.4 m and the focal ratio is 14.4/8.2 ≈ f/1.76. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"a492-v12-07","title":"RC 光學、副鏡五軸與多焦點配置：量測與驗證","titleEn":"RC optics, the five-axis secondary and multiple foci: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"],"prerequisiteIds":["a492-v12-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「Ritchey–Chrétien 光路與焦點」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Ritchey–Chrétien train and foci” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"在 Nasmyth 焦面以波前感測器做副鏡對焦掃描，量離焦項對副鏡位移的斜率，與 (m² + 1) 的預測比較；再以已知角距的星對量測底片比例尺，並在不同仰角重複，分離重力撓曲造成的置中與彗差。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Run a secondary focus scan with the wavefront sensor at the Nasmyth focus, measure the slope of the defocus term versus secondary displacement and compare it with the (m² + 1) prediction; then measure plate scale on star pairs of known separation and repeat at several elevations to separate gravity-flexure-induced decentre and coma. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：副鏡置中誤差會產生與視場無關的固定彗差，若被誤當成主鏡面形誤差而交給主鏡致動器修正，主鏡會被施加不必要的力，並在換仰角後留下新的像差。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: A secondary decentre produces field-constant coma; if it is mistaken for primary figure error and handed to the primary actuators, the primary is loaded with unnecessary forces and new aberrations appear after an elevation change.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a492-v12-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在 Nasmyth 焦面以波前感測器做副鏡對焦掃描，量離焦項對副鏡位移的斜率，與 (m² + 1) 的預測比較；再以已知角距的星對量測底片比例尺，並在不同仰角重複，分離重力撓曲造成的置中與彗差。","textEn":"Run a secondary focus scan with the wavefront sensor at the Nasmyth focus, measure the slope of the defocus term versus secondary displacement and compare it with the (m² + 1) prediction; then measure plate scale on star pairs of known separation and repeat at several elevations to separate gravity-flexure-induced decentre and coma.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]},{"id":"a492-v12-07-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「RC 光學、副鏡五軸與多焦點配置」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"RC optics, the five-axis secondary and multiple foci\"?","options":["沿用另一台設備或另一個案例的量測結果，就可視為本系統已完成驗證。","在 Nasmyth 焦面以波前感測器做副鏡對焦掃描，量離焦項對副鏡位移的斜率，與 (m² + 1) 的預測比較。","鏡面反射率降低幾個百分點，對望遠鏡效能幾乎沒有影響。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another instrument or another case counts as verifying this system.","Run a secondary focus scan with the wavefront sensor at the Nasmyth focus, measure the slope of the defocus term versus secondary displacement and compare it with the (m² + 1) prediction.","A few percent of lost reflectance hardly affects telescope performance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在 Nasmyth 焦面以波前感測器做副鏡對焦掃描，量離焦項對副鏡位移的斜率，與 (m² + 1) 的預測比較；再以已知角距的星對量測底片比例尺，並在不同仰角重複，分離重力撓曲造成的置中與彗差。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Run a secondary focus scan with the wavefront sensor at the Nasmyth focus, measure the slope of the defocus term versus secondary displacement and compare it with the (m² + 1) prediction; then measure plate scale on star pairs of known separation and repeat at several elevations to separate gravity-flexure-induced decentre and coma. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"a492-v12-08","title":"RC 光學、副鏡五軸與多焦點配置：失效診斷","titleEn":"RC optics, the five-axis secondary and multiple foci: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"],"prerequisiteIds":["a492-v12-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「Ritchey–Chrétien 光路與焦點」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Ritchey–Chrétien train and foci” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"副鏡置中誤差會產生與視場無關的固定彗差，若被誤當成主鏡面形誤差而交給主鏡致動器修正，主鏡會被施加不必要的力，並在換仰角後留下新的像差。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"A secondary decentre produces field-constant coma; if it is mistaken for primary figure error and handed to the primary actuators, the primary is loaded with unnecessary forces and new aberrations appear after an elevation change. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：副鏡單元以五個自由度定位：一軸對焦、兩軸置中、兩軸指向；因為副鏡把主鏡焦比放大約 8 倍，副鏡的微小軸向位移會在焦面被放大，所以副鏡對焦是主動光學閉環中最頻繁的修正。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Because the secondary magnifies the primary focal ratio about eightfold, small axial secondary motions are amplified at the focal plane, which makes secondary focus the most frequent correction in the active-optics loop.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「副鏡只是轉折光路的鏡子，位置差幾十微米沒有影響。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The secondary only folds the beam, so tens of micrometres of position error do not matter.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a492-v12-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"副鏡置中誤差會產生與視場無關的固定彗差，若被誤當成主鏡面形誤差而交給主鏡致動器修正，主鏡會被施加不必要的力，並在換仰角後留下新的像差。","textEn":"A secondary decentre produces field-constant coma; if it is mistaken for primary figure error and handed to the primary actuators, the primary is loaded with unnecessary forces and new aberrations appear after an elevation change.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]},{"id":"a492-v12-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「RC 光學、副鏡五軸與多焦點配置」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"RC optics, the five-axis secondary and multiple foci\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["調高增益或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數異常。","主鏡越厚越剛，影像品質就一定越好。","副鏡置中誤差會產生與視場無關的固定彗差，若被誤當成主鏡面形誤差而交給主鏡致動器修正，主鏡會被施加不必要的力，並在換仰角後留下新的像差。"],"optionsEn":["Raising the gain or widening the acceptance limits solves most anomalies.","A thicker, stiffer primary always gives better image quality.","A secondary decentre produces field-constant coma."],"answer":2,"explanation":"副鏡置中誤差會產生與視場無關的固定彗差，若被誤當成主鏡面形誤差而交給主鏡致動器修正，主鏡會被施加不必要的力，並在換仰角後留下新的像差。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A secondary decentre produces field-constant coma; if it is mistaken for primary figure error and handed to the primary actuators, the primary is loaded with unnecessary forces and new aberrations appear after an elevation change. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"a492-v12-s2","title":"元件、材料與製造","titleEn":"Components, materials and fabrication","description":"本階段聚焦「薄主鏡鏡坯、拋光與熱時間常數」與「可變形副鏡：薄殼、音圈致動器與散熱」：先建立機制與定量模型，再設計驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Thin-primary blank, polishing and thermal time constant\" and \"Deformable secondary: thin shell, voice coils and heat removal\": build the mechanism and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"a492-v12-09","title":"薄主鏡鏡坯、拋光與熱時間常數：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Thin-primary blank, polishing and thermal time constant: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"],"prerequisiteIds":["a492-v12-08"],"objective":"說明「8.2 m Zerodur 薄彎月主鏡」如何決定ESO 甚大望遠鏡 VLT的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “8.2 m Zerodur thin meniscus primary” determines the key performance of “ESO Very Large Telescope”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"UT 主鏡是直徑 8.2 m、厚約 177 mm 的 Zerodur 彎月鏡，成品重約 23 t；每片由 SCHOTT 澆鑄約 45 t 的玻璃陶瓷，經約 3 個月退火與 9 個月陶瓷化，膨脹係數規格 0 ± 0.15×10⁻⁶/K，交貨量測約 −0.03 到 −0.04×10⁻⁶/K。REOSC 在模擬最終鏡室的 150 點氣動支撐上研磨拋光，因為薄鏡本身不保形，驗收必須在主動模式下進行：允許致動器以有限的力修正低階面形，交付的波前約 40 nm RMS。薄鏡的另一個好處是熱慣量小，能跟上夜間氣溫，減少鏡面視寧度。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「8.2 m Zerodur 薄彎月主鏡」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Each UT primary is a Zerodur meniscus 8.2 m across and about 177 mm thick, weighing about 23 t finished; SCHOTT cast about 45 t of glass ceramic per blank, followed by roughly 3 months of annealing and 9 months of ceramisation, to a thermal-expansion specification of 0 ± 0.15×10⁻⁶/K, with delivered blanks measuring about −0.03 to −0.04×10⁻⁶/K. REOSC ground and polished on a 150-point pneumatic support that mimics the final cell; because a thin mirror cannot hold its own shape, acceptance is done in active mode, letting actuators correct low-order figure with limited forces, and delivered wavefronts were about 40 nm RMS. The thin mirror's low thermal inertia also lets it follow the night-time air temperature, reducing mirror seeing. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “8.2 m Zerodur thin meniscus primary”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：Zerodur 熱擴散率 κ = k/(ρc) ≈ 1.46/(2530×821) ≈ 7.0×10⁻⁷ m²/s，厚度 t 的熱時間常數 τ ≈ t²/(π²κ)：t = 0.177 m 時約 1.3 h；若用 1:6 厚徑比的傳統鏡（t ≈ 1.37 m）則約 75 h，重量也從 23 t 增加到約 23 × 1367/177 ≈ 178 t。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Zerodur's diffusivity is κ = k/(ρc) ≈ 1.46/(2530×821) ≈ 7.0×10⁻⁷ m²/s, and the thermal time constant of thickness t is τ ≈ t²/(π²κ): about 1.3 h for t = 0.177 m, but about 75 h for a conventional 1:6 mirror (t ≈ 1.37 m), whose mass would also rise from 23 t to about 23 × 1367/177 ≈ 178 t.","failure":"常見誤解：「主鏡越厚越剛，影像品質就一定越好。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A thicker, stiffer primary always gives better image quality.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「8.2 m Zerodur 薄彎月主鏡」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “8.2 m Zerodur thin meniscus primary”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a492-v12-09-k1","title":"薄主鏡鏡坯、拋光與熱時間常數","titleEn":"Thin-primary blank, polishing and thermal time constant","text":"UT 主鏡是直徑 8.2 m、厚約 177 mm 的 Zerodur 彎月鏡，成品重約 23 t；每片由 SCHOTT 澆鑄約 45 t 的玻璃陶瓷，經約 3 個月退火與 9 個月陶瓷化，膨脹係數規格 0 ± 0.15×10⁻⁶/K，交貨量測約 −0.03 到 −0.04×10⁻⁶/K。REOSC 在模擬最終鏡室的 150 點氣動支撐上研磨拋光，因為薄鏡本身不保形，驗收必須在主動模式下進行：允許致動器以有限的力修正低階面形，交付的波前約 40 nm RMS。","textEn":"Each UT primary is a Zerodur meniscus 8.2 m across and about 177 mm thick, weighing about 23 t finished; SCHOTT cast about 45 t of glass ceramic per blank, followed by roughly 3 months of annealing and 9 months of ceramisation, to a thermal-expansion specification of 0 ± 0.15×10⁻⁶/K, with delivered blanks measuring about −0.03 to −0.04×10⁻⁶/K. REOSC ground and polished on a 150-point pneumatic support that mimics the final cell; because a thin mirror cannot hold its own shape, acceptance is done in active mode, letting actuators correct low-order figure with limited forces, and delivered wavefronts were about 40 nm RMS.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]},{"id":"a492-v12-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：主鏡越厚越剛，影像品質就一定越好。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A thicker, stiffer primary always gives better image quality. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「薄主鏡鏡坯、拋光與熱時間常數」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Thin-primary blank, polishing and thermal time constant\" is correct?","options":["UT 主鏡是直徑 8.2 m、厚約 177 mm 的 Zerodur 彎月鏡，成品重約 23 t。","主鏡越厚越剛，影像品質就一定越好。","致動器越多越好，與觀測波長無關。"],"optionsEn":["Each UT primary is a Zerodur meniscus 8.2 m across and about 177 mm thick, weighing about 23 t finished.","A thicker, stiffer primary always gives better image quality.","More actuators are always better, regardless of the observing wavelength."],"answer":0,"explanation":"UT 主鏡是直徑 8.2 m、厚約 177 mm 的 Zerodur 彎月鏡，成品重約 23 t；每片由 SCHOTT 澆鑄約 45 t 的玻璃陶瓷，經約 3 個月退火與 9 個月陶瓷化，膨脹係數規格 0 ± 0.15×10⁻⁶/K，交貨量測約 −0.03 到 −0.04×10⁻⁶/K。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Each UT primary is a Zerodur meniscus 8.2 m across and about 177 mm thick, weighing about 23 t finished; SCHOTT cast about 45 t of glass ceramic per blank, followed by roughly 3 months of annealing and 9 months of ceramisation, to a thermal-expansion specification of 0 ± 0.15×10⁻⁶/K, with delivered blanks measuring about −0.03 to −0.04×10⁻⁶/K. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"a492-v12-10","title":"薄主鏡鏡坯、拋光與熱時間常數：定量估算","titleEn":"Thin-primary blank, polishing and thermal time constant: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"],"prerequisiteIds":["a492-v12-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「8.2 m Zerodur 薄彎月主鏡」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “8.2 m Zerodur thin meniscus primary” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：Zerodur 熱擴散率 κ = k/(ρc) ≈ 1.46/(2530×821) ≈ 7.0×10⁻⁷ m²/s，厚度 t 的熱時間常數 τ ≈ t²/(π²κ)：t = 0.177 m 時約 1.3 h；若用 1:6 厚徑比的傳統鏡（t ≈ 1.37 m）則約 75 h，重量也從 23 t 增加到約 23 × 1367/177 ≈ 178 t。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Zerodur's diffusivity is κ = k/(ρc) ≈ 1.46/(2530×821) ≈ 7.0×10⁻⁷ m²/s, and the thermal time constant of thickness t is τ ≈ t²/(π²κ): about 1.3 h for t = 0.177 m, but about 75 h for a conventional 1:6 mirror (t ≈ 1.37 m), whose mass would also rise from 23 t to about 23 × 1367/177 ≈ 178 t. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：拋光驗收時在多個支撐方位量全口徑干涉相位圖，扣除主動光學可修正的低階模態後計算殘差 RMS、斜率與中心強度比；營運中以鏡面溫度感測器與氣溫的差值追蹤熱平衡，並比對該差值與影像 FWHM 的相關性。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: For polishing acceptance, take full-aperture interferometric phase maps at several support orientations, remove the low-order modes that active optics can correct and compute residual RMS, slope error and central-intensity ratio; in operation, track the mirror-to-air temperature difference with surface sensors and correlate it with image FWHM.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a492-v12-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"Zerodur 熱擴散率 κ = k/(ρc) ≈ 1.46/(2530×821) ≈ 7.0×10⁻⁷ m²/s，厚度 t 的熱時間常數 τ ≈ t²/(π²κ)：t = 0.177 m 時約 1.3 h；若用 1:6 厚徑比的傳統鏡（t ≈ 1.37 m）則約 75 h，重量也從 23 t 增加到約 23 × 1367/177 ≈ 178 t。","textEn":"Zerodur's diffusivity is κ = k/(ρc) ≈ 1.46/(2530×821) ≈ 7.0×10⁻⁷ m²/s, and the thermal time constant of thickness t is τ ≈ t²/(π²κ): about 1.3 h for t = 0.177 m, but about 75 h for a conventional 1:6 mirror (t ≈ 1.37 m), whose mass would also rise from 23 t to about 23 × 1367/177 ≈ 178 t.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]},{"id":"a492-v12-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「薄主鏡鏡坯、拋光與熱時間常數」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Thin-primary blank, polishing and thermal time constant\", which statement holds?","options":["只要基線夠長，干涉儀的角解析度就自動實現，與光程穩定度無關。","Zerodur 熱擴散率 κ = k/(ρc) ≈ 1.46/(2530×821) ≈ 7.0×10⁻⁷ m²/s，厚度 t 的熱時間常數 τ ≈ t²/(π²κ)：t = 0.177 m 時約 1.3 h。","鏡面反射率降低幾個百分點，對望遠鏡效能幾乎沒有影響。"],"optionsEn":["With a long enough baseline the interferometer's resolution is achieved automatically, regardless of path stability.","Zerodur's diffusivity is κ = k/(ρc) ≈ 1.46/(2530×821) ≈ 7.0×10⁻⁷ m²/s, and the thermal time constant of thickness t is τ ≈ t²/(π²κ): about 1.3 h for t = 0.177 m, but about 75 h for a conventional 1:6 mirror (t ≈ 1.37 m), whose mass would also rise from 23 t to about 23 × 1367/177 ≈ 178 t.","A few percent of lost reflectance hardly affects telescope performance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"Zerodur 熱擴散率 κ = k/(ρc) ≈ 1.46/(2530×821) ≈ 7.0×10⁻⁷ m²/s，厚度 t 的熱時間常數 τ ≈ t²/(π²κ)：t = 0.177 m 時約 1.3 h；若用 1:6 厚徑比的傳統鏡（t ≈ 1.37 m）則約 75 h，重量也從 23 t 增加到約 23 × 1367/177 ≈ 178 t。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Zerodur's diffusivity is κ = k/(ρc) ≈ 1.46/(2530×821) ≈ 7.0×10⁻⁷ m²/s, and the thermal time constant of thickness t is τ ≈ t²/(π²κ): about 1.3 h for t = 0.177 m, but about 75 h for a conventional 1:6 mirror (t ≈ 1.37 m), whose mass would also rise from 23 t to about 23 × 1367/177 ≈ 178 t. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"a492-v12-11","title":"薄主鏡鏡坯、拋光與熱時間常數：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Thin-primary blank, polishing and thermal time constant: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"],"prerequisiteIds":["a492-v12-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「8.2 m Zerodur 薄彎月主鏡」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “8.2 m Zerodur thin meniscus primary” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"拋光驗收時在多個支撐方位量全口徑干涉相位圖，扣除主動光學可修正的低階模態後計算殘差 RMS、斜率與中心強度比；營運中以鏡面溫度感測器與氣溫的差值追蹤熱平衡，並比對該差值與影像 FWHM 的相關性。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"For polishing acceptance, take full-aperture interferometric phase maps at several support orientations, remove the low-order modes that active optics can correct and compute residual RMS, slope error and central-intensity ratio; in operation, track the mirror-to-air temperature difference with surface sensors and correlate it with image FWHM. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：支撐點的力誤差或吊運時的局部應力會在薄鏡上直接留下面形印記；若鏡面比夜間空氣溫度高 1 K 以上，鏡面上方形成上升熱羽，影像 FWHM 增加，被誤判為大氣視寧度變差。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: Force errors at support points or local stress during handling print directly into the figure of a thin mirror; if the mirror runs more than about 1 K warmer than the night air, a rising thermal plume forms above it and image FWHM grows, often misread as worse atmospheric seeing.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a492-v12-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"拋光驗收時在多個支撐方位量全口徑干涉相位圖，扣除主動光學可修正的低階模態後計算殘差 RMS、斜率與中心強度比；營運中以鏡面溫度感測器與氣溫的差值追蹤熱平衡，並比對該差值與影像 FWHM 的相關性。","textEn":"For polishing acceptance, take full-aperture interferometric phase maps at several support orientations, remove the low-order modes that active optics can correct and compute residual RMS, slope error and central-intensity ratio; in operation, track the mirror-to-air temperature difference with surface sensors and correlate it with image FWHM.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]},{"id":"a492-v12-11-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「薄主鏡鏡坯、拋光與熱時間常數」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Thin-primary blank, polishing and thermal time constant\"?","options":["只看單次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準件或重複量測。","望遠鏡口徑加倍，地面影像的解析度就一定加倍。","拋光驗收時在多個支撐方位量全口徑干涉相位圖，扣除主動光學可修正的低階模態後計算殘差 RMS、斜率與中心強度比。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the result; no reference artefact or repeat measurement is needed.","Doubling the aperture always doubles the resolution of ground-based images.","For polishing acceptance, take full-aperture interferometric phase maps at several support orientations, remove the low-order modes that active optics can correct and compute residual RMS, slope error and central-intensity ratio."],"answer":2,"explanation":"拋光驗收時在多個支撐方位量全口徑干涉相位圖，扣除主動光學可修正的低階模態後計算殘差 RMS、斜率與中心強度比；營運中以鏡面溫度感測器與氣溫的差值追蹤熱平衡，並比對該差值與影像 FWHM 的相關性。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"For polishing acceptance, take full-aperture interferometric phase maps at several support orientations, remove the low-order modes that active optics can correct and compute residual RMS, slope error and central-intensity ratio; in operation, track the mirror-to-air temperature difference with surface sensors and correlate it with image FWHM. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"a492-v12-12","title":"薄主鏡鏡坯、拋光與熱時間常數：失效診斷","titleEn":"Thin-primary blank, polishing and thermal time constant: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"],"prerequisiteIds":["a492-v12-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「8.2 m Zerodur 薄彎月主鏡」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “8.2 m Zerodur thin meniscus primary” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"支撐點的力誤差或吊運時的局部應力會在薄鏡上直接留下面形印記；若鏡面比夜間空氣溫度高 1 K 以上，鏡面上方形成上升熱羽，影像 FWHM 增加，被誤判為大氣視寧度變差。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"Force errors at support points or local stress during handling print directly into the figure of a thin mirror; if the mirror runs more than about 1 K warmer than the night air, a rising thermal plume forms above it and image FWHM grows, often misread as worse atmospheric seeing. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：薄鏡的另一個好處是熱慣量小，能跟上夜間氣溫，減少鏡面視寧度。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The thin mirror's low thermal inertia also lets it follow the night-time air temperature, reducing mirror seeing.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「主鏡越厚越剛，影像品質就一定越好。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A thicker, stiffer primary always gives better image quality.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a492-v12-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"支撐點的力誤差或吊運時的局部應力會在薄鏡上直接留下面形印記；若鏡面比夜間空氣溫度高 1 K 以上，鏡面上方形成上升熱羽，影像 FWHM 增加，被誤判為大氣視寧度變差。","textEn":"Force errors at support points or local stress during handling print directly into the figure of a thin mirror; if the mirror runs more than about 1 K warmer than the night air, a rising thermal plume forms above it and image FWHM grows, often misread as worse atmospheric seeing.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]},{"id":"a492-v12-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「薄主鏡鏡坯、拋光與熱時間常數」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Thin-primary blank, polishing and thermal time constant\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["支撐點的力誤差或吊運時的局部應力會在薄鏡上直接留下面形印記。","異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","致動器越多越好，與觀測波長無關。"],"optionsEn":["Force errors at support points or local stress during handling print directly into the figure of a thin mirror.","An anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","More actuators are always better, regardless of the observing wavelength."],"answer":0,"explanation":"支撐點的力誤差或吊運時的局部應力會在薄鏡上直接留下面形印記；若鏡面比夜間空氣溫度高 1 K 以上，鏡面上方形成上升熱羽，影像 FWHM 增加，被誤判為大氣視寧度變差。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Force errors at support points or local stress during handling print directly into the figure of a thin mirror; if the mirror runs more than about 1 K warmer than the night air, a rising thermal plume forms above it and image FWHM grows, often misread as worse atmospheric seeing. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"a492-v12-13","title":"可變形副鏡：薄殼、音圈致動器與散熱：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Deformable secondary: thin shell, voice coils and heat removal: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"],"prerequisiteIds":["a492-v12-12"],"objective":"說明「1170 致動器可變形副鏡」如何決定ESO 甚大望遠鏡 VLT的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “1170-actuator deformable secondary” determines the key performance of “ESO Very Large Telescope”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"UT4 的自適應光學設施把原本的剛性副鏡換成直徑 1120 mm、厚約 2 mm 的 Zerodur 薄殼可變形副鏡，背後以 1170 個音圈致動器推動；薄殼由 SAGEM 製作，參考體由 SESO 以輕量化 Zerodur 製造，系統由 Microgate 與 ADS International 整合。每個致動器旁有電容感測器量測薄殼與參考體的約 90 µm 間隙，內迴路以 80 kHz 維持形狀，這層空氣膜同時提供阻尼。把自適應元件放在副鏡，讓所有焦點共用修正且不增加額外反射面與熱背景。致動器與電子機箱的熱必須以液冷帶走，否則副鏡附近形成局部湍流。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「1170 致動器可變形副鏡」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The UT4 Adaptive Optics Facility replaced the rigid secondary with a deformable secondary: a Zerodur shell 1120 mm across and about 2 mm thick, pushed by 1170 voice-coil actuators. SAGEM produced the shell, SESO the lightweighted Zerodur reference body, and Microgate with ADS International integrated the system. A capacitive sensor beside each actuator measures the roughly 90 µm gap between shell and reference body, an internal loop at 80 kHz holds the shape, and the air film provides damping. Putting the adaptive element at the secondary lets all foci share the correction without extra reflections or thermal background. Heat from actuators and electronics must be carried away by liquid cooling, or local turbulence forms around the secondary. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “1170-actuator deformable secondary”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：致動器最小間距約 28 mm，投影到 8.2 m 瞳面約 28 × 8.2/1120 m ≈ 0.205 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The minimum actuator pitch of about 28 mm projects to about 28 × 8.2/1120 m ≈ 0.205 m on the 8.2 m pupil.","failure":"常見誤解：「致動器越多越好，與觀測波長無關。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"More actuators are always better, regardless of the observing wavelength.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「1170 致動器可變形副鏡」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “1170-actuator deformable secondary”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a492-v12-13-k1","title":"可變形副鏡：薄殼、音圈致動器與散熱","titleEn":"Deformable secondary: thin shell, voice coils and heat removal","text":"UT4 的自適應光學設施把原本的剛性副鏡換成直徑 1120 mm、厚約 2 mm 的 Zerodur 薄殼可變形副鏡，背後以 1170 個音圈致動器推動；薄殼由 SAGEM 製作，參考體由 SESO 以輕量化 Zerodur 製造，系統由 Microgate 與 ADS International 整合。每個致動器旁有電容感測器量測薄殼與參考體的約 90 µm 間隙，內迴路以 80 kHz 維持形狀，這層空氣膜同時提供阻尼。","textEn":"The UT4 Adaptive Optics Facility replaced the rigid secondary with a deformable secondary: a Zerodur shell 1120 mm across and about 2 mm thick, pushed by 1170 voice-coil actuators. SAGEM produced the shell, SESO the lightweighted Zerodur reference body, and Microgate with ADS International integrated the system.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]},{"id":"a492-v12-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：致動器越多越好，與觀測波長無關。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: More actuators are always better, regardless of the observing wavelength. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「可變形副鏡：薄殼、音圈致動器與散熱」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Deformable secondary: thin shell, voice coils and heat removal\" is correct?","options":["致動器越多越好，與觀測波長無關。","UT4 的自適應光學設施把原本的剛性副鏡換成直徑 1120 mm、厚約 2 mm 的 Zerodur 薄殼可變形副鏡，背後以 1170 個音圈致動器推動。","有了雷射導引星就完全不需要自然星。"],"optionsEn":["More actuators are always better, regardless of the observing wavelength.","The UT4 Adaptive Optics Facility replaced the rigid secondary with a deformable secondary: a Zerodur shell 1120 mm across and about 2 mm thick, pushed by 1170 voice-coil actuators.","With laser guide stars no natural star is needed at all."],"answer":1,"explanation":"UT4 的自適應光學設施把原本的剛性副鏡換成直徑 1120 mm、厚約 2 mm 的 Zerodur 薄殼可變形副鏡，背後以 1170 個音圈致動器推動；薄殼由 SAGEM 製作，參考體由 SESO 以輕量化 Zerodur 製造，系統由 Microgate 與 ADS International 整合。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The UT4 Adaptive Optics Facility replaced the rigid secondary with a deformable secondary: a Zerodur shell 1120 mm across and about 2 mm thick, pushed by 1170 voice-coil actuators. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"a492-v12-14","title":"可變形副鏡：薄殼、音圈致動器與散熱：定量估算","titleEn":"Deformable secondary: thin shell, voice coils and heat removal: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"],"prerequisiteIds":["a492-v12-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「1170 致動器可變形副鏡」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “1170-actuator deformable secondary” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：致動器最小間距約 28 mm，投影到 8.2 m 瞳面約 28 × 8.2/1120 m ≈ 0.205 m。連續面形的擬合誤差 σ² ≈ 0.28(d/r₀)^5/3：K 波段 r₀ ≈ 0.89 m（由 500 nm 的 0.15 m 以 λ^6/5 換算）時 σ² ≈ 0.024 rad²，只看擬合項 Strehl ≈ 0.98；可見光 r₀ = 0.15 m 時 σ² ≈ 0.47、Strehl ≈ 0.62。散熱 1326 W、流量 4.5 L/min 的水冷液溫升約 4.2 K。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The minimum actuator pitch of about 28 mm projects to about 28 × 8.2/1120 m ≈ 0.205 m on the 8.2 m pupil. The continuous-facesheet fitting error σ² ≈ 0.28(d/r₀)^5/3 gives σ² ≈ 0.024 rad² and a fitting-only Strehl ≈ 0.98 in K band with r₀ ≈ 0.89 m (scaled from 0.15 m at 500 nm by λ^6/5), but σ² ≈ 0.47 and Strehl ≈ 0.62 in the visible with r₀ = 0.15 m. Removing 1326 W with 4.5 L/min of water raises the coolant by about 4.2 K. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：在實驗室以干涉儀量薄殼在每個致動器單位推力下的影響函數，建立影響矩陣並量測平面化後的殘差；上機前用專用測試台以人工光源量閉迴路的擬合誤差與頻寬；上機後比較冷卻液出入口溫差與副鏡周圍的溫度感測器，確認沒有熱羽進入光路。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: In the laboratory measure the shell's influence function for a unit force on each actuator with an interferometer, build the influence matrix and measure the flattened residual; before installation measure closed-loop fitting error and bandwidth on a dedicated test bench with an artificial source; after installation compare coolant inlet-outlet temperatures with sensors around the secondary to make sure no thermal plume enters the beam.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a492-v12-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"致動器最小間距約 28 mm，投影到 8.2 m 瞳面約 28 × 8.2/1120 m ≈ 0.205 m。連續面形的擬合誤差 σ² ≈ 0.28(d/r₀)^5/3：K 波段 r₀ ≈ 0.89 m（由 500 nm 的 0.15 m 以 λ^6/5 換算）時 σ² ≈ 0.024 rad²，只看擬合項 Strehl ≈ 0.98；可見光 r₀ = 0.15 m 時 σ² ≈ 0.47、Strehl ≈ 0.62。散熱 1326 W、流量 4.5 L/min 的水冷液溫升約 4.2 K。","textEn":"The minimum actuator pitch of about 28 mm projects to about 28 × 8.2/1120 m ≈ 0.205 m on the 8.2 m pupil. The continuous-facesheet fitting error σ² ≈ 0.28(d/r₀)^5/3 gives σ² ≈ 0.024 rad² and a fitting-only Strehl ≈ 0.98 in K band with r₀ ≈ 0.89 m (scaled from 0.15 m at 500 nm by λ^6/5), but σ² ≈ 0.47 and Strehl ≈ 0.62 in the visible with r₀ = 0.15 m. Removing 1326 W with 4.5 L/min of water raises the coolant by about 4.2 K.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]},{"id":"a492-v12-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「可變形副鏡：薄殼、音圈致動器與散熱」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Deformable secondary: thin shell, voice coils and heat removal\", which statement holds?","options":["只要解析度夠高，徑向速度精度就不受儀器穩定度限制。","望遠鏡口徑加倍，地面影像的解析度就一定加倍。","致動器最小間距約 28 mm，投影到 8.2 m 瞳面約 28 × 8.2/1120 m ≈ 0.205 m。"],"optionsEn":["With high enough resolving power, radial-velocity precision is not limited by instrument stability.","Doubling the aperture always doubles the resolution of ground-based images.","The minimum actuator pitch of about 28 mm projects to about 28 × 8.2/1120 m ≈ 0.205 m on the 8.2 m pupil."],"answer":2,"explanation":"致動器最小間距約 28 mm，投影到 8.2 m 瞳面約 28 × 8.2/1120 m ≈ 0.205 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The minimum actuator pitch of about 28 mm projects to about 28 × 8.2/1120 m ≈ 0.205 m on the 8.2 m pupil. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"a492-v12-15","title":"可變形副鏡：薄殼、音圈致動器與散熱：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Deformable secondary: thin shell, voice coils and heat removal: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"],"prerequisiteIds":["a492-v12-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「1170 致動器可變形副鏡」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “1170-actuator deformable secondary” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"在實驗室以干涉儀量薄殼在每個致動器單位推力下的影響函數，建立影響矩陣並量測平面化後的殘差；上機前用專用測試台以人工光源量閉迴路的擬合誤差與頻寬；上機後比較冷卻液出入口溫差與副鏡周圍的溫度感測器，確認沒有熱羽進入光路。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"In the laboratory measure the shell's influence function for a unit force on each actuator with an interferometer, build the influence matrix and measure the flattened residual; before installation measure closed-loop fitting error and bandwidth on a dedicated test bench with an artificial source; after installation compare coolant inlet-outlet temperatures with sensors around the secondary to make sure no thermal plume enters the beam. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：灰塵或顆粒卡在 90 µm 間隙中會讓局部致動器無法到位，薄殼出現凸點甚至破裂；冷卻流量不足時，電子機箱發熱使副鏡附近溫度上升，影像品質在自適應光學閉迴路中仍無法改善。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: Dust or particles caught in the 90 µm gap stop local actuators from reaching position, leaving a bump or even cracking the shell; with insufficient coolant flow, electronics heat raises the temperature near the secondary and image quality fails to improve even with the AO loop closed.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a492-v12-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在實驗室以干涉儀量薄殼在每個致動器單位推力下的影響函數，建立影響矩陣並量測平面化後的殘差；上機前用專用測試台以人工光源量閉迴路的擬合誤差與頻寬；上機後比較冷卻液出入口溫差與副鏡周圍的溫度感測器，確認沒有熱羽進入光路。","textEn":"In the laboratory measure the shell's influence function for a unit force on each actuator with an interferometer, build the influence matrix and measure the flattened residual; before installation measure closed-loop fitting error and bandwidth on a dedicated test bench with an artificial source; after installation compare coolant inlet-outlet temperatures with sensors around the secondary to make sure no thermal plume enters the beam.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]},{"id":"a492-v12-15-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「可變形副鏡：薄殼、音圈致動器與散熱」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Deformable secondary: thin shell, voice coils and heat removal\"?","options":["在實驗室以干涉儀量薄殼在每個致動器單位推力下的影響函數，建立影響矩陣並量測平面化後的殘差。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","副鏡只是轉折光路的鏡子，位置差幾十微米沒有影響。"],"optionsEn":["In the laboratory measure the shell's influence function for a unit force on each actuator with an interferometer, build the influence matrix and measure the flattened residual.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","The secondary only folds the beam, so tens of micrometres of position error do not matter."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在實驗室以干涉儀量薄殼在每個致動器單位推力下的影響函數，建立影響矩陣並量測平面化後的殘差；上機前用專用測試台以人工光源量閉迴路的擬合誤差與頻寬；上機後比較冷卻液出入口溫差與副鏡周圍的溫度感測器，確認沒有熱羽進入光路。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"In the laboratory measure the shell's influence function for a unit force on each actuator with an interferometer, build the influence matrix and measure the flattened residual; before installation measure closed-loop fitting error and bandwidth on a dedicated test bench with an artificial source; after installation compare coolant inlet-outlet temperatures with sensors around the secondary to make sure no thermal plume enters the beam. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"a492-v12-16","title":"可變形副鏡：薄殼、音圈致動器與散熱：失效診斷","titleEn":"Deformable secondary: thin shell, voice coils and heat removal: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"],"prerequisiteIds":["a492-v12-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「1170 致動器可變形副鏡」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “1170-actuator deformable secondary” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"灰塵或顆粒卡在 90 µm 間隙中會讓局部致動器無法到位，薄殼出現凸點甚至破裂；冷卻流量不足時，電子機箱發熱使副鏡附近溫度上升，影像品質在自適應光學閉迴路中仍無法改善。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"Dust or particles caught in the 90 µm gap stop local actuators from reaching position, leaving a bump or even cracking the shell; with insufficient coolant flow, electronics heat raises the temperature near the secondary and image quality fails to improve even with the AO loop closed. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：致動器與電子機箱的熱必須以液冷帶走，否則副鏡附近形成局部湍流。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Heat from actuators and electronics must be carried away by liquid cooling, or local turbulence forms around the secondary.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「致動器越多越好，與觀測波長無關。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"More actuators are always better, regardless of the observing wavelength.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a492-v12-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"灰塵或顆粒卡在 90 µm 間隙中會讓局部致動器無法到位，薄殼出現凸點甚至破裂；冷卻流量不足時，電子機箱發熱使副鏡附近溫度上升，影像品質在自適應光學閉迴路中仍無法改善。","textEn":"Dust or particles caught in the 90 µm gap stop local actuators from reaching position, leaving a bump or even cracking the shell; with insufficient coolant flow, electronics heat raises the temperature near the secondary and image quality fails to improve even with the AO loop closed.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]},{"id":"a492-v12-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「可變形副鏡：薄殼、音圈致動器與散熱」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Deformable secondary: thin shell, voice coils and heat removal\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的零件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","灰塵或顆粒卡在 90 µm 間隙中會讓局部致動器無法到位，薄殼出現凸點甚至破裂。","有了雷射導引星就完全不需要自然星。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive part first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Dust or particles caught in the 90 µm gap stop local actuators from reaching position, leaving a bump or even cracking the shell.","With laser guide stars no natural star is needed at all."],"answer":1,"explanation":"灰塵或顆粒卡在 90 µm 間隙中會讓局部致動器無法到位，薄殼出現凸點甚至破裂；冷卻流量不足時，電子機箱發熱使副鏡附近溫度上升，影像品質在自適應光學閉迴路中仍無法改善。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Dust or particles caught in the 90 µm gap stop local actuators from reaching position, leaving a bump or even cracking the shell; with insufficient coolant flow, electronics heat raises the temperature near the secondary and image quality fails to improve even with the AO loop closed. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"a492-v12-s3","title":"量測、校正與誤差預算","titleEn":"Measurement, calibration and error budgets","description":"本階段聚焦「雷射導引星、地表層修正與光點拉長」與「VLTI 基線、延遲線與光程差預算」：先建立機制與定量模型，再設計驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Laser guide stars, ground-layer correction and spot elongation\" and \"VLTI baselines, delay lines and the OPD budget\": build the mechanism and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"a492-v12-17","title":"雷射導引星、地表層修正與光點拉長：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Laser guide stars, ground-layer correction and spot elongation: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"],"prerequisiteIds":["a492-v12-16"],"objective":"說明「四雷射導引星設施」如何決定ESO 甚大望遠鏡 VLT的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Four Laser Guide Star Facility” determines the key performance of “ESO Very Large Telescope”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"自然亮星很少落在目標附近，因此 UT4 以四雷射導引星設施在約 90 km 高的鈉層激發四顆人造星。四顆導引星環繞視場，GRAAL 模組把地表層湍流修正後的影像送給 HAWK-I，GALACSI 則為 MUSE 做地表層或雷射斷層修正。雷射星位於有限高度，光錐只取樣部分湍流（錐效應），且鈉層有約 10 km 厚度，從望遠鏡不同位置看到的雷射光點會被拉長，次孔徑離發射點越遠拉得越長。雷射星也無法量測整體傾斜，所以仍需要一顆暗的自然星提供傾斜資訊。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「四雷射導引星設施」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Bright natural stars rarely lie near a target, so UT4 uses the Four Laser Guide Star Facility to excite four artificial stars in the sodium layer at about 90 km. The four guide stars surround the field; the GRAAL module feeds ground-layer-corrected images to HAWK-I, and GALACSI provides ground-layer or laser-tomography correction for MUSE. Because a laser star sits at finite altitude, its light cone samples only part of the turbulence (the cone effect), and because the sodium layer is about 10 km thick, the spot seen from different parts of the pupil is elongated, more so for subapertures farther from the launch point. Laser stars also cannot measure overall tilt, so a faint natural star is still needed for tip-tilt. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Four Laser Guide Star Facility”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：光點拉長角 ≈ b·Δh/H²：次孔徑距發射點 b = 8 m（假設）、鈉層厚 Δh = 10 km、高度 H = 90 km 時，拉長 ≈ 8 × 10⁴/(9×10⁴)² ≈ 9.9×10⁻⁶ rad ≈ 2.0″，遠大於次孔徑繞射寬度，量測斜率的雜訊因而在拉長方向變大。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Spot elongation ≈ b·Δh/H²: for a subaperture b = 8 m from the launch point (assumption), a 10 km thick sodium layer at H = 90 km gives ≈ 8 × 10⁴/(9×10⁴)² ≈ 9.9×10⁻⁶ rad ≈ 2.0″, far wider than a subaperture's diffraction width, so slope noise grows along the elongation direction.","failure":"常見誤解：「有了雷射導引星就完全不需要自然星。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"With laser guide stars no natural star is needed at all.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「四雷射導引星設施」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Four Laser Guide Star Facility”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a492-v12-17-k1","title":"雷射導引星、地表層修正與光點拉長","titleEn":"Laser guide stars, ground-layer correction and spot elongation","text":"自然亮星很少落在目標附近，因此 UT4 以四雷射導引星設施在約 90 km 高的鈉層激發四顆人造星。四顆導引星環繞視場，GRAAL 模組把地表層湍流修正後的影像送給 HAWK-I，GALACSI 則為 MUSE 做地表層或雷射斷層修正。","textEn":"Bright natural stars rarely lie near a target, so UT4 uses the Four Laser Guide Star Facility to excite four artificial stars in the sodium layer at about 90 km. The four guide stars surround the field; the GRAAL module feeds ground-layer-corrected images to HAWK-I, and GALACSI provides ground-layer or laser-tomography correction for MUSE.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]},{"id":"a492-v12-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：有了雷射導引星就完全不需要自然星。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: With laser guide stars no natural star is needed at all. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「雷射導引星、地表層修正與光點拉長」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Laser guide stars, ground-layer correction and spot elongation\" is correct?","options":["有了雷射導引星就完全不需要自然星。","只要基線夠長，干涉儀的角解析度就自動實現，與光程穩定度無關。","自然亮星很少落在目標附近，因此 UT4 以四雷射導引星設施在約 90 km 高的鈉層激發四顆人造星。"],"optionsEn":["With laser guide stars no natural star is needed at all.","With a long enough baseline the interferometer's resolution is achieved automatically, regardless of path stability.","Bright natural stars rarely lie near a target, so UT4 uses the Four Laser Guide Star Facility to excite four artificial stars in the sodium layer at about 90 km."],"answer":2,"explanation":"自然亮星很少落在目標附近，因此 UT4 以四雷射導引星設施在約 90 km 高的鈉層激發四顆人造星。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Bright natural stars rarely lie near a target, so UT4 uses the Four Laser Guide Star Facility to excite four artificial stars in the sodium layer at about 90 km. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"a492-v12-18","title":"雷射導引星、地表層修正與光點拉長：定量估算","titleEn":"Laser guide stars, ground-layer correction and spot elongation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"],"prerequisiteIds":["a492-v12-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「四雷射導引星設施」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Four Laser Guide Star Facility” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：光點拉長角 ≈ b·Δh/H²：次孔徑距發射點 b = 8 m（假設）、鈉層厚 Δh = 10 km、高度 H = 90 km 時，拉長 ≈ 8 × 10⁴/(9×10⁴)² ≈ 9.9×10⁻⁶ rad ≈ 2.0″，遠大於次孔徑繞射寬度，量測斜率的雜訊因而在拉長方向變大。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Spot elongation ≈ b·Δh/H²: for a subaperture b = 8 m from the launch point (assumption), a 10 km thick sodium layer at H = 90 km gives ≈ 8 × 10⁴/(9×10⁴)² ≈ 9.9×10⁻⁶ rad ≈ 2.0″, far wider than a subaperture's diffraction width, so slope noise grows along the elongation direction. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：以波前感測器影像量各次孔徑雷射光點的長軸與短軸寬度，對次孔徑到發射點的距離作圖，檢查是否符合 b·Δh/H² 的線性關係並反推鈉層厚度；再與同時段的鈉層剖面或回波強度紀錄比對，確認重心演算法的加權設定。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure long- and short-axis widths of the laser spot in each subaperture from wavefront-sensor frames, plot them against distance from the launch point to check the linear b·Δh/H² relation and back out the sodium-layer thickness; compare with contemporaneous sodium-profile or return-flux records to confirm the weighting used by the centroid algorithm.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a492-v12-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"光點拉長角 ≈ b·Δh/H²：次孔徑距發射點 b = 8 m（假設）、鈉層厚 Δh = 10 km、高度 H = 90 km 時，拉長 ≈ 8 × 10⁴/(9×10⁴)² ≈ 9.9×10⁻⁶ rad ≈ 2.0″，遠大於次孔徑繞射寬度，量測斜率的雜訊因而在拉長方向變大。","textEn":"Spot elongation ≈ b·Δh/H²: for a subaperture b = 8 m from the launch point (assumption), a 10 km thick sodium layer at H = 90 km gives ≈ 8 × 10⁴/(9×10⁴)² ≈ 9.9×10⁻⁶ rad ≈ 2.0″, far wider than a subaperture's diffraction width, so slope noise grows along the elongation direction.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]},{"id":"a492-v12-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「雷射導引星、地表層修正與光點拉長」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Laser guide stars, ground-layer correction and spot elongation\", which statement holds?","options":["光點拉長角 ≈ b·Δh/H²：次孔徑距發射點 b = 8 m（假設）、鈉層厚 Δh = 10 km、高度 H = 90 km 時，拉長 ≈ 8 × 10⁴/(9×10⁴)² ≈ 9.9×10⁻⁶ rad ≈ 2.0″，遠大於次孔徑繞射寬度，量測斜率的雜訊因而在拉長方向變大。","鏡面反射率降低幾個百分點，對望遠鏡效能幾乎沒有影響。","副鏡只是轉折光路的鏡子，位置差幾十微米沒有影響。"],"optionsEn":["Spot elongation ≈ b·Δh/H²: for a subaperture b = 8 m from the launch point (assumption), a 10 km thick sodium layer at H = 90 km gives ≈ 8 × 10⁴/(9×10⁴)² ≈ 9.9×10⁻⁶ rad ≈ 2.0″, far wider than a subaperture's diffraction width, so slope noise grows along the elongation direction.","A few percent of lost reflectance hardly affects telescope performance.","The secondary only folds the beam, so tens of micrometres of position error do not matter."],"answer":0,"explanation":"光點拉長角 ≈ b·Δh/H²：次孔徑距發射點 b = 8 m（假設）、鈉層厚 Δh = 10 km、高度 H = 90 km 時，拉長 ≈ 8 × 10⁴/(9×10⁴)² ≈ 9.9×10⁻⁶ rad ≈ 2.0″，遠大於次孔徑繞射寬度，量測斜率的雜訊因而在拉長方向變大。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Spot elongation ≈ b·Δh/H²: for a subaperture b = 8 m from the launch point (assumption), a 10 km thick sodium layer at H = 90 km gives ≈ 8 × 10⁴/(9×10⁴)² ≈ 9.9×10⁻⁶ rad ≈ 2.0″, far wider than a subaperture's diffraction width, so slope noise grows along the elongation direction. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"a492-v12-19","title":"雷射導引星、地表層修正與光點拉長：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Laser guide stars, ground-layer correction and spot elongation: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"],"prerequisiteIds":["a492-v12-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「四雷射導引星設施」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Four Laser Guide Star Facility” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"以波前感測器影像量各次孔徑雷射光點的長軸與短軸寬度，對次孔徑到發射點的距離作圖，檢查是否符合 b·Δh/H² 的線性關係並反推鈉層厚度；再與同時段的鈉層剖面或回波強度紀錄比對，確認重心演算法的加權設定。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure long- and short-axis widths of the laser spot in each subaperture from wavefront-sensor frames, plot them against distance from the launch point to check the linear b·Δh/H² relation and back out the sodium-layer thickness; compare with contemporaneous sodium-profile or return-flux records to confirm the weighting used by the centroid algorithm. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：鈉層高度在夜間變化數公里時，雷射星的對焦也跟著改變；若沒有以自然星的慢速對焦感測修正，系統會把鈉層高度變化誤當成望遠鏡離焦，科學影像持續失焦。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: When the sodium-layer altitude changes by kilometres during the night, the laser-star focus changes with it; without slow natural-star focus sensing, the system interprets sodium-height changes as telescope defocus and the science image stays out of focus.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a492-v12-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以波前感測器影像量各次孔徑雷射光點的長軸與短軸寬度，對次孔徑到發射點的距離作圖，檢查是否符合 b·Δh/H² 的線性關係並反推鈉層厚度；再與同時段的鈉層剖面或回波強度紀錄比對，確認重心演算法的加權設定。","textEn":"Measure long- and short-axis widths of the laser spot in each subaperture from wavefront-sensor frames, plot them against distance from the launch point to check the linear b·Δh/H² relation and back out the sodium-layer thickness; compare with contemporaneous sodium-profile or return-flux records to confirm the weighting used by the centroid algorithm.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]},{"id":"a492-v12-19-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「雷射導引星、地表層修正與光點拉長」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Laser guide stars, ground-layer correction and spot elongation\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","以波前感測器影像量各次孔徑雷射光點的長軸與短軸寬度，對次孔徑到發射點的距離作圖，檢查是否符合 b·Δh/H² 的線性關係並反推鈉層厚度。","主鏡越厚越剛，影像品質就一定越好。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Measure long- and short-axis widths of the laser spot in each subaperture from wavefront-sensor frames, plot them against distance from the launch point to check the linear b·Δh/H² relation and back out the sodium-layer thickness.","A thicker, stiffer primary always gives better image quality."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以波前感測器影像量各次孔徑雷射光點的長軸與短軸寬度，對次孔徑到發射點的距離作圖，檢查是否符合 b·Δh/H² 的線性關係並反推鈉層厚度；再與同時段的鈉層剖面或回波強度紀錄比對，確認重心演算法的加權設定。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure long- and short-axis widths of the laser spot in each subaperture from wavefront-sensor frames, plot them against distance from the launch point to check the linear b·Δh/H² relation and back out the sodium-layer thickness; compare with contemporaneous sodium-profile or return-flux records to confirm the weighting used by the centroid algorithm. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"a492-v12-20","title":"雷射導引星、地表層修正與光點拉長：失效診斷","titleEn":"Laser guide stars, ground-layer correction and spot elongation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"],"prerequisiteIds":["a492-v12-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「四雷射導引星設施」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Four Laser Guide Star Facility” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"鈉層高度在夜間變化數公里時，雷射星的對焦也跟著改變；若沒有以自然星的慢速對焦感測修正，系統會把鈉層高度變化誤當成望遠鏡離焦，科學影像持續失焦。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"When the sodium-layer altitude changes by kilometres during the night, the laser-star focus changes with it; without slow natural-star focus sensing, the system interprets sodium-height changes as telescope defocus and the science image stays out of focus. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：雷射星也無法量測整體傾斜，所以仍需要一顆暗的自然星提供傾斜資訊。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Laser stars also cannot measure overall tilt, so a faint natural star is still needed for tip-tilt.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「有了雷射導引星就完全不需要自然星。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"With laser guide stars no natural star is needed at all.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a492-v12-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"鈉層高度在夜間變化數公里時，雷射星的對焦也跟著改變；若沒有以自然星的慢速對焦感測修正，系統會把鈉層高度變化誤當成望遠鏡離焦，科學影像持續失焦。","textEn":"When the sodium-layer altitude changes by kilometres during the night, the laser-star focus changes with it; without slow natural-star focus sensing, the system interprets sodium-height changes as telescope defocus and the science image stays out of focus.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]},{"id":"a492-v12-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「雷射導引星、地表層修正與光點拉長」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Laser guide stars, ground-layer correction and spot elongation\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","只要基線夠長，干涉儀的角解析度就自動實現，與光程穩定度無關。","鈉層高度在夜間變化數公里時，雷射星的對焦也跟著改變；若沒有以自然星的慢速對焦感測修正，系統會把鈉層高度變化誤當成望遠鏡離焦，科學影像持續失焦。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","With a long enough baseline the interferometer's resolution is achieved automatically, regardless of path stability.","When the sodium-layer altitude changes by kilometres during the night, the laser-star focus changes with it."],"answer":2,"explanation":"鈉層高度在夜間變化數公里時，雷射星的對焦也跟著改變；若沒有以自然星的慢速對焦感測修正，系統會把鈉層高度變化誤當成望遠鏡離焦，科學影像持續失焦。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"When the sodium-layer altitude changes by kilometres during the night, the laser-star focus changes with it; without slow natural-star focus sensing, the system interprets sodium-height changes as telescope defocus and the science image stays out of focus. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"a492-v12-21","title":"VLTI 基線、延遲線與光程差預算：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"VLTI baselines, delay lines and the OPD budget: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"],"prerequisiteIds":["a492-v12-20"],"objective":"說明「VLTI 延遲線隧道」如何決定ESO 甚大望遠鏡 VLT的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “VLTI delay-line tunnel” determines the key performance of “ESO Very Large Telescope”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"VLTI 把兩到四座望遠鏡的光經地下光管送到延遲線，延遲線是放在長軌道上的貓眼反射車，隨地球自轉連續移動以補償幾何光程差，使各路光在合光器處等光程而產生干涉條紋。UT 間基線可達約 130 m，輔助望遠鏡可移到不同基座組成約 200 m 的基線。條紋對比（可見度）攜帶目標的空間頻率資訊，但只要各路光程差抖動接近波長的十分之一，可見度就明顯下降；GRAVITY 等儀器以條紋追蹤器在 K 波段即時量測並回授到延遲線，再以雷射計量量測內部光程。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「VLTI 延遲線隧道」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"VLTI sends light from two to four telescopes through underground light ducts to the delay lines, cat's-eye carriages on long rails that move continuously with Earth rotation to cancel the geometric path difference so that all beams arrive at the combiner with equal path and form fringes. Baselines between UTs reach about 130 m, and the Auxiliary Telescopes can be moved between stations to form baselines of about 200 m. Fringe contrast (visibility) carries the target's spatial-frequency information, but once the path-difference jitter approaches a tenth of the wavelength the visibility drops markedly; instruments such as GRAVITY measure fringes in K band with a fringe tracker that feeds back to the delay lines, and laser metrology measures internal paths. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “VLTI delay-line tunnel”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：幾何延遲變化率最大約 B·Ω⊕：B = 130 m 時 130 × 7.29×10⁻⁵ rad/s ≈ 9.5 mm/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The geometric delay rate peaks near B·Ω⊕: for B = 130 m, 130 × 7.29×10⁻⁵ rad/s ≈ 9.5 mm/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要基線夠長，干涉儀的角解析度就自動實現，與光程穩定度無關。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"With a long enough baseline the interferometer's resolution is achieved automatically, regardless of path stability.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「VLTI 延遲線隧道」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “VLTI delay-line tunnel”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a492-v12-21-k1","title":"VLTI 基線、延遲線與光程差預算","titleEn":"VLTI baselines, delay lines and the OPD budget","text":"VLTI 把兩到四座望遠鏡的光經地下光管送到延遲線，延遲線是放在長軌道上的貓眼反射車，隨地球自轉連續移動以補償幾何光程差，使各路光在合光器處等光程而產生干涉條紋。UT 間基線可達約 130 m，輔助望遠鏡可移到不同基座組成約 200 m 的基線。","textEn":"VLTI sends light from two to four telescopes through underground light ducts to the delay lines, cat's-eye carriages on long rails that move continuously with Earth rotation to cancel the geometric path difference so that all beams arrive at the combiner with equal path and form fringes. Baselines between UTs reach about 130 m, and the Auxiliary Telescopes can be moved between stations to form baselines of about 200 m.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]},{"id":"a492-v12-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要基線夠長，干涉儀的角解析度就自動實現，與光程穩定度無關。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: With a long enough baseline the interferometer's resolution is achieved automatically, regardless of path stability. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「VLTI 基線、延遲線與光程差預算」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"VLTI baselines, delay lines and the OPD budget\" is correct?","options":["VLTI 把兩到四座望遠鏡的光經地下光管送到延遲線，延遲線是放在長軌道上的貓眼反射車，隨地球自轉連續移動以補償幾何光程差，使各路光在合光器處等光程而產生干涉條紋。","只要基線夠長，干涉儀的角解析度就自動實現，與光程穩定度無關。","只要解析度夠高，徑向速度精度就不受儀器穩定度限制。"],"optionsEn":["VLTI sends light from two to four telescopes through underground light ducts to the delay lines, cat's-eye carriages on long rails that move continuously with Earth rotation to cancel the geometric path difference so that all beams arrive at the combiner with equal path and form fringes.","With a long enough baseline the interferometer's resolution is achieved automatically, regardless of path stability.","With high enough resolving power, radial-velocity precision is not limited by instrument stability."],"answer":0,"explanation":"VLTI 把兩到四座望遠鏡的光經地下光管送到延遲線，延遲線是放在長軌道上的貓眼反射車，隨地球自轉連續移動以補償幾何光程差，使各路光在合光器處等光程而產生干涉條紋。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"VLTI sends light from two to four telescopes through underground light ducts to the delay lines, cat's-eye carriages on long rails that move continuously with Earth rotation to cancel the geometric path difference so that all beams arrive at the combiner with equal path and form fringes. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"a492-v12-22","title":"VLTI 基線、延遲線與光程差預算：定量估算","titleEn":"VLTI baselines, delay lines and the OPD budget: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"],"prerequisiteIds":["a492-v12-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「VLTI 延遲線隧道」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “VLTI delay-line tunnel” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：幾何延遲變化率最大約 B·Ω⊕：B = 130 m 時 130 × 7.29×10⁻⁵ rad/s ≈ 9.5 mm/s。K 波段角解析度 λ/(2B) ≈ 2.2 µm/260 m ≈ 1.7 mas，200 m 時約 1.1 mas。光程差抖動 σ = 150 nm 時相位抖動 2πσ/λ ≈ 0.43 rad，可見度衰減因子 exp(−σφ²/2) ≈ 0.91。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The geometric delay rate peaks near B·Ω⊕: for B = 130 m, 130 × 7.29×10⁻⁵ rad/s ≈ 9.5 mm/s. K-band resolution λ/(2B) ≈ 2.2 µm/260 m ≈ 1.7 mas, and about 1.1 mas at 200 m. An OPD jitter σ = 150 nm gives phase jitter 2πσ/λ ≈ 0.43 rad and a visibility loss factor exp(−σφ²/2) ≈ 0.91. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：以內部光源量測各延遲線的光程差功率譜，找出機械共振與振動源；在天上觀測已知直徑的校準星，比較量到的可見度與預期值得到系統傳遞函數，再以望遠鏡上的加速度計量測各鏡面振動，追蹤哪一座望遠鏡貢獻最多光程差抖動。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure the OPD power spectrum of each delay line with an internal source to locate mechanical resonances and vibration sources; observe calibrator stars of known diameter and compare measured with expected visibility to obtain the system transfer function; use accelerometers on the telescope mirrors to track which telescope contributes most of the OPD jitter.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a492-v12-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"幾何延遲變化率最大約 B·Ω⊕：B = 130 m 時 130 × 7.29×10⁻⁵ rad/s ≈ 9.5 mm/s。K 波段角解析度 λ/(2B) ≈ 2.2 µm/260 m ≈ 1.7 mas，200 m 時約 1.1 mas。光程差抖動 σ = 150 nm 時相位抖動 2πσ/λ ≈ 0.43 rad，可見度衰減因子 exp(−σφ²/2) ≈ 0.91。","textEn":"The geometric delay rate peaks near B·Ω⊕: for B = 130 m, 130 × 7.29×10⁻⁵ rad/s ≈ 9.5 mm/s. K-band resolution λ/(2B) ≈ 2.2 µm/260 m ≈ 1.7 mas, and about 1.1 mas at 200 m. An OPD jitter σ = 150 nm gives phase jitter 2πσ/λ ≈ 0.43 rad and a visibility loss factor exp(−σφ²/2) ≈ 0.91.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]},{"id":"a492-v12-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「VLTI 基線、延遲線與光程差預算」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"VLTI baselines, delay lines and the OPD budget\", which statement holds?","options":["望遠鏡口徑加倍，地面影像的解析度就一定加倍。","幾何延遲變化率最大約 B·Ω⊕：B = 130 m 時 130 × 7.29×10⁻⁵ rad/s ≈ 9.5 mm/s。","主鏡越厚越剛，影像品質就一定越好。"],"optionsEn":["Doubling the aperture always doubles the resolution of ground-based images.","The geometric delay rate peaks near B·Ω⊕: for B = 130 m, 130 × 7.29×10⁻⁵ rad/s ≈ 9.5 mm/s.","A thicker, stiffer primary always gives better image quality."],"answer":1,"explanation":"幾何延遲變化率最大約 B·Ω⊕：B = 130 m 時 130 × 7.29×10⁻⁵ rad/s ≈ 9.5 mm/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The geometric delay rate peaks near B·Ω⊕: for B = 130 m, 130 × 7.29×10⁻⁵ rad/s ≈ 9.5 mm/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"a492-v12-23","title":"VLTI 基線、延遲線與光程差預算：量測與驗證","titleEn":"VLTI baselines, delay lines and the OPD budget: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"],"prerequisiteIds":["a492-v12-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「VLTI 延遲線隧道」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “VLTI delay-line tunnel” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"以內部光源量測各延遲線的光程差功率譜，找出機械共振與振動源；在天上觀測已知直徑的校準星，比較量到的可見度與預期值得到系統傳遞函數，再以望遠鏡上的加速度計量測各鏡面振動，追蹤哪一座望遠鏡貢獻最多光程差抖動。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure the OPD power spectrum of each delay line with an internal source to locate mechanical resonances and vibration sources; observe calibrator stars of known diameter and compare measured with expected visibility to obtain the system transfer function; use accelerometers on the telescope mirrors to track which telescope contributes most of the OPD jitter. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：機房泵浦或冷卻機的數十 Hz 振動經基座傳到鏡面，光程差抖動達數百奈米，條紋追蹤器跟不上而反覆失鎖，可見度被系統性壓低，若不以校準星修正，會被誤解為目標被解析。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: Pump or chiller vibration at tens of hertz travels through the foundations to the mirrors and drives hundreds of nanometres of OPD jitter; the fringe tracker repeatedly loses lock and visibilities are systematically depressed, which without calibrator correction is misread as a resolved target.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a492-v12-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以內部光源量測各延遲線的光程差功率譜，找出機械共振與振動源；在天上觀測已知直徑的校準星，比較量到的可見度與預期值得到系統傳遞函數，再以望遠鏡上的加速度計量測各鏡面振動，追蹤哪一座望遠鏡貢獻最多光程差抖動。","textEn":"Measure the OPD power spectrum of each delay line with an internal source to locate mechanical resonances and vibration sources; observe calibrator stars of known diameter and compare measured with expected visibility to obtain the system transfer function; use accelerometers on the telescope mirrors to track which telescope contributes most of the OPD jitter.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]},{"id":"a492-v12-23-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「VLTI 基線、延遲線與光程差預算」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"VLTI baselines, delay lines and the OPD budget\"?","options":["只要模擬結果看起來合理，就可以省略實體量測與校正。","致動器越多越好，與觀測波長無關。","以內部光源量測各延遲線的光程差功率譜，找出機械共振與振動源。"],"optionsEn":["If the simulation looks reasonable, physical measurement and calibration can be skipped.","More actuators are always better, regardless of the observing wavelength.","Measure the OPD power spectrum of each delay line with an internal source to locate mechanical resonances and vibration sources."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以內部光源量測各延遲線的光程差功率譜，找出機械共振與振動源；在天上觀測已知直徑的校準星，比較量到的可見度與預期值得到系統傳遞函數，再以望遠鏡上的加速度計量測各鏡面振動，追蹤哪一座望遠鏡貢獻最多光程差抖動。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure the OPD power spectrum of each delay line with an internal source to locate mechanical resonances and vibration sources; observe calibrator stars of known diameter and compare measured with expected visibility to obtain the system transfer function; use accelerometers on the telescope mirrors to track which telescope contributes most of the OPD jitter. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"a492-v12-24","title":"VLTI 基線、延遲線與光程差預算：失效診斷","titleEn":"VLTI baselines, delay lines and the OPD budget: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"],"prerequisiteIds":["a492-v12-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「VLTI 延遲線隧道」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “VLTI delay-line tunnel” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"機房泵浦或冷卻機的數十 Hz 振動經基座傳到鏡面，光程差抖動達數百奈米，條紋追蹤器跟不上而反覆失鎖，可見度被系統性壓低，若不以校準星修正，會被誤解為目標被解析。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"Pump or chiller vibration at tens of hertz travels through the foundations to the mirrors and drives hundreds of nanometres of OPD jitter; the fringe tracker repeatedly loses lock and visibilities are systematically depressed, which without calibrator correction is misread as a resolved target. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：條紋對比（可見度）攜帶目標的空間頻率資訊，但只要各路光程差抖動接近波長的十分之一，可見度就明顯下降；GRAVITY 等儀器以條紋追蹤器在 K 波段即時量測並回授到延遲線，再以雷射計量量測內部光程。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Fringe contrast (visibility) carries the target's spatial-frequency information, but once the path-difference jitter approaches a tenth of the wavelength the visibility drops markedly; instruments such as GRAVITY measure fringes in K band with a fringe tracker that feeds back to the delay lines, and laser metrology measures internal paths.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要基線夠長，干涉儀的角解析度就自動實現，與光程穩定度無關。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"With a long enough baseline the interferometer's resolution is achieved automatically, regardless of path stability.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a492-v12-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"機房泵浦或冷卻機的數十 Hz 振動經基座傳到鏡面，光程差抖動達數百奈米，條紋追蹤器跟不上而反覆失鎖，可見度被系統性壓低，若不以校準星修正，會被誤解為目標被解析。","textEn":"Pump or chiller vibration at tens of hertz travels through the foundations to the mirrors and drives hundreds of nanometres of OPD jitter; the fringe tracker repeatedly loses lock and visibilities are systematically depressed, which without calibrator correction is misread as a resolved target.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]},{"id":"a492-v12-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「VLTI 基線、延遲線與光程差預算」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"VLTI baselines, delay lines and the OPD budget\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["機房泵浦或冷卻機的數十 Hz 振動經基座傳到鏡面，光程差抖動達數百奈米，條紋追蹤器跟不上而反覆失鎖，可見度被系統性壓低，若不以校準星修正，會被誤解為目標被解析。","只要重新開機或重設軟體，硬體失效也會一併排除。","只要解析度夠高，徑向速度精度就不受儀器穩定度限制。"],"optionsEn":["Pump or chiller vibration at tens of hertz travels through the foundations to the mirrors and drives hundreds of nanometres of OPD jitter.","Restarting or resetting the software also clears hardware failures.","With high enough resolving power, radial-velocity precision is not limited by instrument stability."],"answer":0,"explanation":"機房泵浦或冷卻機的數十 Hz 振動經基座傳到鏡面，光程差抖動達數百奈米，條紋追蹤器跟不上而反覆失鎖，可見度被系統性壓低，若不以校準星修正，會被誤解為目標被解析。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Pump or chiller vibration at tens of hertz travels through the foundations to the mirrors and drives hundreds of nanometres of OPD jitter; the fringe tracker repeatedly loses lock and visibilities are systematically depressed, which without calibrator correction is misread as a resolved target. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"a492-v12-s4","title":"系統整合、驗證與工程交接","titleEn":"Integration, validation and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「coudé 光路與 10 cm/s 徑向速度量測」與「多望遠鏡營運：主鏡重鍍、通量與交接」：先建立機制與定量模型，再設計驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Coudé trains and 10 cm/s radial-velocity measurement\" and \"Multi-telescope operation: recoating, throughput and handoff\": build the mechanism and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"a492-v12-25","title":"coudé 光路與 10 cm/s 徑向速度量測：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Coudé trains and 10 cm/s radial-velocity measurement: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"],"prerequisiteIds":["a492-v12-24"],"objective":"說明「ESPRESSO 與合併 coudé 實驗室」如何決定ESO 甚大望遠鏡 VLT的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “ESPRESSO and the combined coudé laboratory” determines the key performance of “ESO Very Large Telescope”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"ESPRESSO 位於合併 coudé 實驗室，可經 coudé 光路收單一 UT 的光，或同時收四座 UT 的光（非同調合併），以換取更暗目標的訊雜比。它的目標是在十年尺度上達到 10 cm/s 的徑向速度精度，解析度依模式約 70,000、140,000 或 190,000。要量到如此小的都卜勒位移，光譜儀必須放在真空、毫開爾文級溫控的環境中，以光纖與散射器穩定照明，並以頻率梳或 Fabry–Pérot 標準具同時記錄波長參考；望遠鏡端的導星與大氣色散補償則決定光纖入口的照明穩定性。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「ESPRESSO 與合併 coudé 實驗室」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"ESPRESSO sits in the combined coudé laboratory and receives light from one UT through its coudé train, or from all four UTs at once (incoherent combination) to gain signal-to-noise on fainter targets. Its goal is 10 cm/s radial-velocity precision over a decade, with resolving power of about 70,000, 140,000 or 190,000 depending on mode. Measuring such tiny Doppler shifts requires the spectrograph to sit in vacuum with millikelvin-class temperature control, fibre feeds with scramblers to stabilise illumination, and a frequency comb or Fabry–Pérot etalon recorded simultaneously as wavelength reference; guiding and atmospheric-dispersion correction at the telescope set how stable the fibre entrance illumination is. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “ESPRESSO and the combined coudé laboratory”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：Δλ/λ = v/c：v = 0.10 m/s 在 550 nm 時 Δλ ≈ 550 nm × 3.3×10⁻¹⁰ ≈ 1.8×10⁻¹⁶ m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Δλ/λ = v/c: v = 0.10 m/s at 550 nm gives Δλ ≈ 550 nm × 3.3×10⁻¹⁰ ≈ 1.8×10⁻¹⁶ m.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要解析度夠高，徑向速度精度就不受儀器穩定度限制。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"With high enough resolving power, radial-velocity precision is not limited by instrument stability.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「ESPRESSO 與合併 coudé 實驗室」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “ESPRESSO and the combined coudé laboratory”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a492-v12-25-k1","title":"coudé 光路與 10 cm/s 徑向速度量測","titleEn":"Coudé trains and 10 cm/s radial-velocity measurement","text":"ESPRESSO 位於合併 coudé 實驗室，可經 coudé 光路收單一 UT 的光，或同時收四座 UT 的光（非同調合併），以換取更暗目標的訊雜比。它的目標是在十年尺度上達到 10 cm/s 的徑向速度精度，解析度依模式約 70,000、140,000 或 190,000。","textEn":"ESPRESSO sits in the combined coudé laboratory and receives light from one UT through its coudé train, or from all four UTs at once (incoherent combination) to gain signal-to-noise on fainter targets. Its goal is 10 cm/s radial-velocity precision over a decade, with resolving power of about 70,000, 140,000 or 190,000 depending on mode.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]},{"id":"a492-v12-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要解析度夠高，徑向速度精度就不受儀器穩定度限制。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: With high enough resolving power, radial-velocity precision is not limited by instrument stability. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「coudé 光路與 10 cm/s 徑向速度量測」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Coudé trains and 10 cm/s radial-velocity measurement\" is correct?","options":["只要解析度夠高，徑向速度精度就不受儀器穩定度限制。","ESPRESSO 位於合併 coudé 實驗室，可經 coudé 光路收單一 UT 的光，或同時收四座 UT 的光（非同調合併），以換取更暗目標的訊雜比。","鏡面反射率降低幾個百分點，對望遠鏡效能幾乎沒有影響。"],"optionsEn":["With high enough resolving power, radial-velocity precision is not limited by instrument stability.","ESPRESSO sits in the combined coudé laboratory and receives light from one UT through its coudé train, or from all four UTs at once (incoherent combination) to gain signal-to-noise on fainter targets.","A few percent of lost reflectance hardly affects telescope performance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"ESPRESSO 位於合併 coudé 實驗室，可經 coudé 光路收單一 UT 的光，或同時收四座 UT 的光（非同調合併），以換取更暗目標的訊雜比。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"ESPRESSO sits in the combined coudé laboratory and receives light from one UT through its coudé train, or from all four UTs at once (incoherent combination) to gain signal-to-noise on fainter targets. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"a492-v12-26","title":"coudé 光路與 10 cm/s 徑向速度量測：定量估算","titleEn":"Coudé trains and 10 cm/s radial-velocity measurement: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"],"prerequisiteIds":["a492-v12-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「ESPRESSO 與合併 coudé 實驗室」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “ESPRESSO and the combined coudé laboratory” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：Δλ/λ = v/c：v = 0.10 m/s 在 550 nm 時 Δλ ≈ 550 nm × 3.3×10⁻¹⁰ ≈ 1.8×10⁻¹⁶ m。R = 140,000 的解析元素為 3.9 pm，若以 4 像素取樣，每像素約 0.98 pm，位移只有 1.9×10⁻⁴ 像素；以 15 µm 像素計約 2.8 nm 的焦面位移。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Δλ/λ = v/c: v = 0.10 m/s at 550 nm gives Δλ ≈ 550 nm × 3.3×10⁻¹⁰ ≈ 1.8×10⁻¹⁶ m. At R = 140,000 the resolution element is 3.9 pm; sampled by 4 pixels, each pixel spans about 0.98 pm, so the shift is only 1.9×10⁻⁴ pixel, about 2.8 nm on the focal plane for 15 µm pixels. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：以同時參考通道記錄頻率梳或標準具譜線的漂移，與科學通道的漂移相減；長期觀測已知穩定的標準星，計算數月到數年的徑向速度散佈，並以太陽或標準星的晝夜資料檢查是否有與溫度、壓力或光纖照明相關的系統項。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record the drift of comb or etalon lines in the simultaneous reference channel and subtract it from the science-channel drift; monitor standard stars known to be quiet over months to years and compute the radial-velocity scatter, checking solar or standard-star data for systematics correlated with temperature, pressure or fibre illumination.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a492-v12-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"Δλ/λ = v/c：v = 0.10 m/s 在 550 nm 時 Δλ ≈ 550 nm × 3.3×10⁻¹⁰ ≈ 1.8×10⁻¹⁶ m。R = 140,000 的解析元素為 3.9 pm，若以 4 像素取樣，每像素約 0.98 pm，位移只有 1.9×10⁻⁴ 像素；以 15 µm 像素計約 2.8 nm 的焦面位移。","textEn":"Δλ/λ = v/c: v = 0.10 m/s at 550 nm gives Δλ ≈ 550 nm × 3.3×10⁻¹⁰ ≈ 1.8×10⁻¹⁶ m. At R = 140,000 the resolution element is 3.9 pm; sampled by 4 pixels, each pixel spans about 0.98 pm, so the shift is only 1.9×10⁻⁴ pixel, about 2.8 nm on the focal plane for 15 µm pixels.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]},{"id":"a492-v12-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「coudé 光路與 10 cm/s 徑向速度量測」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Coudé trains and 10 cm/s radial-velocity measurement\", which statement holds?","options":["副鏡只是轉折光路的鏡子，位置差幾十微米沒有影響。","致動器越多越好，與觀測波長無關。","Δλ/λ = v/c：v = 0.10 m/s 在 550 nm 時 Δλ ≈ 550 nm × 3.3×10⁻¹⁰ ≈ 1.8×10⁻¹⁶ m。"],"optionsEn":["The secondary only folds the beam, so tens of micrometres of position error do not matter.","More actuators are always better, regardless of the observing wavelength.","Δλ/λ = v/c: v = 0.10 m/s at 550 nm gives Δλ ≈ 550 nm × 3.3×10⁻¹⁰ ≈ 1.8×10⁻¹⁶ m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Δλ/λ = v/c：v = 0.10 m/s 在 550 nm 時 Δλ ≈ 550 nm × 3.3×10⁻¹⁰ ≈ 1.8×10⁻¹⁶ m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Δλ/λ = v/c: v = 0.10 m/s at 550 nm gives Δλ ≈ 550 nm × 3.3×10⁻¹⁰ ≈ 1.8×10⁻¹⁶ m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"a492-v12-27","title":"coudé 光路與 10 cm/s 徑向速度量測：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Coudé trains and 10 cm/s radial-velocity measurement: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"],"prerequisiteIds":["a492-v12-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「ESPRESSO 與合併 coudé 實驗室」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “ESPRESSO and the combined coudé laboratory” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"以同時參考通道記錄頻率梳或標準具譜線的漂移，與科學通道的漂移相減；長期觀測已知穩定的標準星，計算數月到數年的徑向速度散佈，並以太陽或標準星的晝夜資料檢查是否有與溫度、壓力或光纖照明相關的系統項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record the drift of comb or etalon lines in the simultaneous reference channel and subtract it from the science-channel drift; monitor standard stars known to be quiet over months to years and compute the radial-velocity scatter, checking solar or standard-star data for systematics correlated with temperature, pressure or fibre illumination. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：導星偏差讓星像在光纖入口移動，若散射不足，光譜線輪廓隨之改變，產生數十 cm/s 的假速度訊號；真空槽溫度漂移 0.01 K 也可透過光柵與鏡座膨脹造成同量級的偏移，被誤認為行星訊號。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: Guiding errors move the star on the fibre entrance; with insufficient scrambling the line profile changes and produces spurious velocities of tens of cm/s, and a 0.01 K drift of the vacuum vessel can cause shifts of similar size through grating and mount expansion that are mistaken for a planet signal.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a492-v12-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以同時參考通道記錄頻率梳或標準具譜線的漂移，與科學通道的漂移相減；長期觀測已知穩定的標準星，計算數月到數年的徑向速度散佈，並以太陽或標準星的晝夜資料檢查是否有與溫度、壓力或光纖照明相關的系統項。","textEn":"Record the drift of comb or etalon lines in the simultaneous reference channel and subtract it from the science-channel drift; monitor standard stars known to be quiet over months to years and compute the radial-velocity scatter, checking solar or standard-star data for systematics correlated with temperature, pressure or fibre illumination.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]},{"id":"a492-v12-27-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「coudé 光路與 10 cm/s 徑向速度量測」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Coudé trains and 10 cm/s radial-velocity measurement\"?","options":["以同時參考通道記錄頻率梳或標準具譜線的漂移，與科學通道的漂移相減。","量測時不必記錄溫度、振動與時間等條件，因為它們不會影響結果。","有了雷射導引星就完全不需要自然星。"],"optionsEn":["Record the drift of comb or etalon lines in the simultaneous reference channel and subtract it from the science-channel drift.","Temperature, vibration and timing need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","With laser guide stars no natural star is needed at all."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以同時參考通道記錄頻率梳或標準具譜線的漂移，與科學通道的漂移相減；長期觀測已知穩定的標準星，計算數月到數年的徑向速度散佈，並以太陽或標準星的晝夜資料檢查是否有與溫度、壓力或光纖照明相關的系統項。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record the drift of comb or etalon lines in the simultaneous reference channel and subtract it from the science-channel drift; monitor standard stars known to be quiet over months to years and compute the radial-velocity scatter, checking solar or standard-star data for systematics correlated with temperature, pressure or fibre illumination. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"a492-v12-28","title":"coudé 光路與 10 cm/s 徑向速度量測：失效診斷","titleEn":"Coudé trains and 10 cm/s radial-velocity measurement: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"],"prerequisiteIds":["a492-v12-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「ESPRESSO 與合併 coudé 實驗室」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “ESPRESSO and the combined coudé laboratory” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"導星偏差讓星像在光纖入口移動，若散射不足，光譜線輪廓隨之改變，產生數十 cm/s 的假速度訊號；真空槽溫度漂移 0.01 K 也可透過光柵與鏡座膨脹造成同量級的偏移，被誤認為行星訊號。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"Guiding errors move the star on the fibre entrance; with insufficient scrambling the line profile changes and produces spurious velocities of tens of cm/s, and a 0.01 K drift of the vacuum vessel can cause shifts of similar size through grating and mount expansion that are mistaken for a planet signal. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：要量到如此小的都卜勒位移，光譜儀必須放在真空、毫開爾文級溫控的環境中，以光纖與散射器穩定照明，並以頻率梳或 Fabry–Pérot 標準具同時記錄波長參考；望遠鏡端的導星與大氣色散補償則決定光纖入口的照明穩定性。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Measuring such tiny Doppler shifts requires the spectrograph to sit in vacuum with millikelvin-class temperature control, fibre feeds with scramblers to stabilise illumination, and a frequency comb or Fabry–Pérot etalon recorded simultaneously as wavelength reference; guiding and atmospheric-dispersion correction at the telescope set how stable the fibre entrance illumination is.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要解析度夠高，徑向速度精度就不受儀器穩定度限制。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"With high enough resolving power, radial-velocity precision is not limited by instrument stability.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a492-v12-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"導星偏差讓星像在光纖入口移動，若散射不足，光譜線輪廓隨之改變，產生數十 cm/s 的假速度訊號；真空槽溫度漂移 0.01 K 也可透過光柵與鏡座膨脹造成同量級的偏移，被誤認為行星訊號。","textEn":"Guiding errors move the star on the fibre entrance; with insufficient scrambling the line profile changes and produces spurious velocities of tens of cm/s, and a 0.01 K drift of the vacuum vessel can cause shifts of similar size through grating and mount expansion that are mistaken for a planet signal.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]},{"id":"a492-v12-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「coudé 光路與 10 cm/s 徑向速度量測」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Coudé trains and 10 cm/s radial-velocity measurement\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自操作人員失誤，系統設計不需要檢討。","導星偏差讓星像在光纖入口移動，若散射不足，光譜線輪廓隨之改變，產生數十 cm/s 的假速度訊號。","鏡面反射率降低幾個百分點，對望遠鏡效能幾乎沒有影響。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is operator error, so the system design never needs review.","Guiding errors move the star on the fibre entrance.","A few percent of lost reflectance hardly affects telescope performance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"導星偏差讓星像在光纖入口移動，若散射不足，光譜線輪廓隨之改變，產生數十 cm/s 的假速度訊號；真空槽溫度漂移 0.01 K 也可透過光柵與鏡座膨脹造成同量級的偏移，被誤認為行星訊號。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Guiding errors move the star on the fibre entrance; with insufficient scrambling the line profile changes and produces spurious velocities of tens of cm/s, and a 0.01 K drift of the vacuum vessel can cause shifts of similar size through grating and mount expansion that are mistaken for a planet signal. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"a492-v12-29","title":"多望遠鏡營運：主鏡重鍍、通量與交接：原理與系統邊界","titleEn":"Multi-telescope operation: recoating, throughput and handoff: mechanism and system boundary","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"],"prerequisiteIds":["a492-v12-28"],"objective":"說明「主鏡單元維護與鍍膜」如何決定ESO 甚大望遠鏡 VLT的關鍵性能，並畫出其輸入、輸出與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Primary-mirror unit maintenance and coating” determines the key performance of “ESO Very Large Telescope”, and map its inputs, outputs and boundaries.","instruction":"四座 UT 各有不同焦點的常駐儀器，營運上要協調哪座望遠鏡做 VLTI、哪座做自適應光學、哪座提供 coudé 光，維護計畫也必須錯開。主鏡單元約 50 t，需從望遠鏡卸下送到山上的鍍膜廠清洗並重鍍鋁膜；灰塵沉積會逐步降低反射率並增加熱輻射背景，對中紅外儀器尤其不利。交接紀錄要包含每座望遠鏡的影像品質、主動光學力圖、自適應光學性能、延遲線狀態與反射率歷史，才能讓下一個觀測期的排程以實際能力為準。 師傅任務：以方塊圖畫出能量或訊號通過「主鏡單元維護與鍍膜」的路徑，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由環境或製造決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The four UTs carry resident instruments at different foci, so operations must coordinate which telescope serves VLTI, which runs adaptive optics and which feeds the coudé laboratory, and maintenance must be staggered. The roughly 50 t primary-mirror unit is removed from the telescope and taken to the on-site coating plant for cleaning and aluminium recoating; dust gradually lowers reflectance and raises thermal background, which hurts mid-infrared instruments in particular. The handoff record must include each telescope's image quality, active-optics force maps, AO performance, delay-line status and reflectance history so that the next period's schedule rests on actual capability. Mentor task: draw a block diagram of the energy or signal path through “Primary-mirror unit maintenance and coating”, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by environment or fabrication, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：Nasmyth 光路經 M1、M2、M3 三次反射。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The Nasmyth train has three reflections, M1, M2 and M3.","failure":"常見誤解：「鏡面反射率降低幾個百分點，對望遠鏡效能幾乎沒有影響。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在方塊圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A few percent of lost reflectance hardly affects telescope performance.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your block diagram where it breaks down.","check":"方塊圖標明「主鏡單元維護與鍍膜」的輸入、輸出與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The block diagram shows inputs, outputs and boundaries of “Primary-mirror unit maintenance and coating”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"a492-v12-29-k1","title":"多望遠鏡營運：主鏡重鍍、通量與交接","titleEn":"Multi-telescope operation: recoating, throughput and handoff","text":"四座 UT 各有不同焦點的常駐儀器，營運上要協調哪座望遠鏡做 VLTI、哪座做自適應光學、哪座提供 coudé 光，維護計畫也必須錯開。主鏡單元約 50 t，需從望遠鏡卸下送到山上的鍍膜廠清洗並重鍍鋁膜；灰塵沉積會逐步降低反射率並增加熱輻射背景，對中紅外儀器尤其不利。","textEn":"The four UTs carry resident instruments at different foci, so operations must coordinate which telescope serves VLTI, which runs adaptive optics and which feeds the coudé laboratory, and maintenance must be staggered. The roughly 50 t primary-mirror unit is removed from the telescope and taken to the on-site coating plant for cleaning and aluminium recoating; dust gradually lowers reflectance and raises thermal background, which hurts mid-infrared instruments in particular.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]},{"id":"a492-v12-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：鏡面反射率降低幾個百分點，對望遠鏡效能幾乎沒有影響。 正確的工程判斷必須回到機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A few percent of lost reflectance hardly affects telescope performance. Sound engineering judgement goes back to mechanism and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「多望遠鏡營運：主鏡重鍍、通量與交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Multi-telescope operation: recoating, throughput and handoff\" is correct?","options":["鏡面反射率降低幾個百分點，對望遠鏡效能幾乎沒有影響。","望遠鏡口徑加倍，地面影像的解析度就一定加倍。","四座 UT 各有不同焦點的常駐儀器，營運上要協調哪座望遠鏡做 VLTI、哪座做自適應光學、哪座提供 coudé 光，維護計畫也必須錯開。"],"optionsEn":["A few percent of lost reflectance hardly affects telescope performance.","Doubling the aperture always doubles the resolution of ground-based images.","The four UTs carry resident instruments at different foci, so operations must coordinate which telescope serves VLTI, which runs adaptive optics and which feeds the coudé laboratory, and maintenance must be staggered."],"answer":2,"explanation":"四座 UT 各有不同焦點的常駐儀器，營運上要協調哪座望遠鏡做 VLTI、哪座做自適應光學、哪座提供 coudé 光，維護計畫也必須錯開。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The four UTs carry resident instruments at different foci, so operations must coordinate which telescope serves VLTI, which runs adaptive optics and which feeds the coudé laboratory, and maintenance must be staggered. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"a492-v12-30","title":"多望遠鏡營運：主鏡重鍍、通量與交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Multi-telescope operation: recoating, throughput and handoff: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"],"prerequisiteIds":["a492-v12-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「主鏡單元維護與鍍膜」的關鍵量，並判斷參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Primary-mirror unit maintenance and coating” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of changes when a parameter moves.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：Nasmyth 光路經 M1、M2、M3 三次反射。新鍍鋁膜反射率取 0.92（假設）時通量 0.92³ ≈ 0.779；每面因灰塵降到 0.90 時為 0.90³ ≈ 0.729，同樣訊雜比所需積分時間增加約 0.779/0.729 ≈ 1.068 倍，即約 7%。中紅外每面發射率若因灰塵從 0.02 增至 0.03（假設），三面合計約從 0.06 增至 0.09，10 µm 熱背景增加約 50%。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The Nasmyth train has three reflections, M1, M2 and M3. With freshly coated aluminium at 0.92 reflectance (assumption) throughput is 0.92³ ≈ 0.779; if dust lowers each to 0.90 it becomes 0.90³ ≈ 0.729, so integration time for the same signal-to-noise grows by about 0.779/0.729 ≈ 1.068, about 7%. If dust raises the mid-infrared emissivity of each mirror from 0.02 to 0.03 (assumption), the three-mirror total grows from about 0.06 to 0.09 and the 10 µm thermal background by about 50%. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, and state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper.","observation":"如何核對：以攜帶式反射率計定期量測主鏡多個位置的反射率與散射，並以標準星的光度零點追蹤整體通量；重鍍後重新量測主動光學力圖與影像品質，確認卸裝與再安裝沒有改變支撐與對準，再把結果寫入營運交接紀錄。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure reflectance and scatter at several points on the primary periodically with a portable reflectometer and track overall throughput through photometric zero points of standard stars; after recoating, remeasure active-optics force maps and image quality to confirm that removal and reinstallation did not change support or alignment, and enter the results in the operational handoff record.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成設備規格，或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit conversion slips, treating teaching assumptions as equipment specifications, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與物理解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with a physical explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"a492-v12-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"Nasmyth 光路經 M1、M2、M3 三次反射。新鍍鋁膜反射率取 0.92（假設）時通量 0.92³ ≈ 0.779；每面因灰塵降到 0.90 時為 0.90³ ≈ 0.729，同樣訊雜比所需積分時間增加約 0.779/0.729 ≈ 1.068 倍，即約 7%。中紅外每面發射率若因灰塵從 0.02 增至 0.03（假設），三面合計約從 0.06 增至 0.09，10 µm 熱背景增加約 50%。","textEn":"The Nasmyth train has three reflections, M1, M2 and M3. With freshly coated aluminium at 0.92 reflectance (assumption) throughput is 0.92³ ≈ 0.779; if dust lowers each to 0.90 it becomes 0.90³ ≈ 0.729, so integration time for the same signal-to-noise grows by about 0.779/0.729 ≈ 1.068, about 7%. If dust raises the mid-infrared emissivity of each mirror from 0.02 to 0.03 (assumption), the three-mirror total grows from about 0.06 to 0.09 and the 10 µm thermal background by about 50%.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]},{"id":"a492-v12-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設；套用到實際設備前，必須重新取得規格、操作條件與不確定度。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions; before applying them to real equipment, obtain the actual specifications, operating conditions and uncertainties.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「多望遠鏡營運：主鏡重鍍、通量與交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Multi-telescope operation: recoating, throughput and handoff\", which statement holds?","options":["Nasmyth 光路經 M1、M2、M3 三次反射。","主鏡越厚越剛，影像品質就一定越好。","有了雷射導引星就完全不需要自然星。"],"optionsEn":["The Nasmyth train has three reflections, M1, M2 and M3.","A thicker, stiffer primary always gives better image quality.","With laser guide stars no natural star is needed at all."],"answer":0,"explanation":"Nasmyth 光路經 M1、M2、M3 三次反射。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The Nasmyth train has three reflections, M1, M2 and M3. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"a492-v12-31","title":"多望遠鏡營運：主鏡重鍍、通量與交接：量測與驗證","titleEn":"Multi-telescope operation: recoating, throughput and handoff: measurement and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"],"prerequisiteIds":["a492-v12-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的量測，驗證「主鏡單元維護與鍍膜」是否符合模型預期，並訂出允收準則。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable measurement that verifies whether “Primary-mirror unit maintenance and coating” meets the model expectation, and set acceptance criteria.","instruction":"以攜帶式反射率計定期量測主鏡多個位置的反射率與散射，並以標準星的光度零點追蹤整體通量；重鍍後重新量測主動光學力圖與影像品質，確認卸裝與再安裝沒有改變支撐與對準，再把結果寫入營運交接紀錄。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成量測計畫，列出儀器、基準件或參考樣品、步驟、比較對象與允收準則，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure reflectance and scatter at several points on the primary periodically with a portable reflectometer and track overall throughput through photometric zero points of standard stars; after recoating, remeasure active-optics force maps and image quality to confirm that removal and reinstallation did not change support or alignment, and enter the results in the operational handoff record. Mentor task: turn this into a measurement plan listing instruments, reference artefacts or samples, procedure, comparison baseline and acceptance criteria, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"注意干擾：重鍍排程若只看反射率而不看中紅外背景，熱紅外儀器的靈敏度會在數月內悄悄下降；主鏡重新安裝後若沒有重做主動光學查表，早期觀測會帶著殘餘像散，浪費寶貴的觀測時段。","observationEn":"Watch for interference: If recoating is scheduled on reflectance alone and ignores mid-infrared background, thermal-infrared sensitivity quietly degrades over months; if active-optics look-up tables are not redone after reinstallation, early observations carry residual astigmatism and waste valuable observing time.","failure":"驗證陷阱：只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄環境條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Verification traps: a single measurement, no traceable reference, or unrecorded environmental conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格。","checkEn":"Submit the measurement plan: instruments, reference, procedure, acceptance criteria and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail decision rule.","knowledge":[{"id":"a492-v12-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以攜帶式反射率計定期量測主鏡多個位置的反射率與散射，並以標準星的光度零點追蹤整體通量；重鍍後重新量測主動光學力圖與影像品質，確認卸裝與再安裝沒有改變支撐與對準，再把結果寫入營運交接紀錄。","textEn":"Measure reflectance and scatter at several points on the primary periodically with a portable reflectometer and track overall throughput through photometric zero points of standard stars; after recoating, remeasure active-optics force maps and image quality to confirm that removal and reinstallation did not change support or alignment, and enter the results in the operational handoff record.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]},{"id":"a492-v12-31-k2","title":"允收與不確定度","titleEn":"Acceptance and uncertainty","text":"允收準則必須在量測前訂定，並與擴充不確定度一起陳述；比較基準需可追溯。","textEn":"Acceptance criteria are fixed before measuring and stated together with expanded uncertainty; the comparison reference must be traceable.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「多望遠鏡營運：主鏡重鍍、通量與交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Multi-telescope operation: recoating, throughput and handoff\"?","options":["沿用另一台設備或另一個案例的量測結果，就可視為本系統已完成驗證。","以攜帶式反射率計定期量測主鏡多個位置的反射率與散射，並以標準星的光度零點追蹤整體通量。","只要基線夠長，干涉儀的角解析度就自動實現，與光程穩定度無關。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another instrument or another case counts as verifying this system.","Measure reflectance and scatter at several points on the primary periodically with a portable reflectometer and track overall throughput through photometric zero points of standard stars.","With a long enough baseline the interferometer's resolution is achieved automatically, regardless of path stability."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以攜帶式反射率計定期量測主鏡多個位置的反射率與散射，並以標準星的光度零點追蹤整體通量；重鍍後重新量測主動光學力圖與影像品質，確認卸裝與再安裝沒有改變支撐與對準，再把結果寫入營運交接紀錄。 驗證需要基準、重複性與允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure reflectance and scatter at several points on the primary periodically with a portable reflectometer and track overall throughput through photometric zero points of standard stars; after recoating, remeasure active-optics force maps and image quality to confirm that removal and reinstallation did not change support or alignment, and enter the results in the operational handoff record. Verification needs a reference, repeatability and acceptance criteria."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"a492-v12-32","title":"多望遠鏡營運：主鏡重鍍、通量與交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Multi-telescope operation: recoating, throughput and handoff: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"],"prerequisiteIds":["a492-v12-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「主鏡單元維護與鍍膜」的失效原因，提出能區分原因的檢查與矯正措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure causes of “Primary-mirror unit maintenance and coating” and propose discriminating checks and corrective actions.","instruction":"重鍍排程若只看反射率而不看中紅外背景，熱紅外儀器的靈敏度會在數月內悄悄下降；主鏡重新安裝後若沒有重做主動光學查表，早期觀測會帶著殘餘像散，浪費寶貴的觀測時段。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整個系統的性能、良率或安全。","instructionEn":"If recoating is scheduled on reflectance alone and ignores mid-infrared background, thermal-infrared sensitivity quietly degrades over months; if active-optics look-up tables are not redone after reinstallation, early observations carry residual astigmatism and waste valuable observing time. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system performance, yield or safety.","observation":"連結機制：交接紀錄要包含每座望遠鏡的影像品質、主動光學力圖、自適應光學性能、延遲線狀態與反射率歷史，才能讓下一個觀測期的排程以實際能力為準。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The handoff record must include each telescope's image quality, active-optics force maps, AO performance, delay-line status and reflectance history so that the next period's schedule rests on actual capability.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「鏡面反射率降低幾個百分點，對望遠鏡效能幾乎沒有影響。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A few percent of lost reflectance hardly affects telescope performance.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，並指出哪一項量測能最快確認根因、如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement that confirms the root cause fastest, and state how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"a492-v12-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"重鍍排程若只看反射率而不看中紅外背景，熱紅外儀器的靈敏度會在數月內悄悄下降；主鏡重新安裝後若沒有重做主動光學查表，早期觀測會帶著殘餘像散，浪費寶貴的觀測時段。","textEn":"If recoating is scheduled on reflectance alone and ignores mid-infrared background, thermal-infrared sensitivity quietly degrades over months; if active-optics look-up tables are not redone after reinstallation, early observations carry residual astigmatism and waste valuable observing time.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]},{"id":"a492-v12-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測確認；只更換零件或放寬參數可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement; merely swapping parts or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「多望遠鏡營運：主鏡重鍍、通量與交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Multi-telescope operation: recoating, throughput and handoff\" misbehaves, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["調高增益或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數異常。","望遠鏡口徑加倍，地面影像的解析度就一定加倍。","重鍍排程若只看反射率而不看中紅外背景，熱紅外儀器的靈敏度會在數月內悄悄下降；主鏡重新安裝後若沒有重做主動光學查表，早期觀測會帶著殘餘像散，浪費寶貴的觀測時段。"],"optionsEn":["Raising the gain or widening the acceptance limits solves most anomalies.","Doubling the aperture always doubles the resolution of ground-based images.","If recoating is scheduled on reflectance alone and ignores mid-infrared background, thermal-infrared sensitivity quietly degrades over months."],"answer":2,"explanation":"重鍍排程若只看反射率而不看中紅外背景，熱紅外儀器的靈敏度會在數月內悄悄下降；主鏡重新安裝後若沒有重做主動光學查表，早期觀測會帶著殘餘像散，浪費寶貴的觀測時段。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"If recoating is scheduled on reflectance alone and ignores mid-infrared background, thermal-infrared sensitivity quietly degrades over months; if active-optics look-up tables are not redone after reinstallation, early observations carry residual astigmatism and waste valuable observing time. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4}],"sourceIds":["v12o-eso-vlt-unit-telescopes","v12o-eso-vlt-primary-mirrors","v12o-eso-vlt-dsm","v12o-eso-espresso-instrument"],"curriculumVersion":12,"stepCount":32,"estimatedMinutes":800}};
